export const AGREEMENTS = {"PA-FAA-2026-11":{"title":"PlotArt Founding Artist Agreement","html":"<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en-IE\"><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n<title>PlotArt Founding Artist Agreement · PA-FAA-2026-11</title><meta name=\"robots\" content=\"noindex, nofollow\">\n<style>\n:root{color-scheme:light}body{margin:0;background:#F4F1EC;color:#1B1C1E;font:16px/1.6 Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif}\nmain{max-width:46rem;margin:0 auto;padding:2.5rem 1rem 4rem}.eyebrow{margin:0;color:#AE6245;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.18em;font-size:.8rem}\nh1{font:400 2.1rem/1.15 Georgia,serif;margin:.3rem 0 .4rem}.sub{margin:0 0 2rem;color:#5E5A55;font-size:.95rem}\nh2{font:400 1.3rem/1.3 Georgia,serif;margin:2.2rem 0 .7rem}p{margin:0 0 .8rem}.cl{display:grid;grid-template-columns:3rem minmax(0,1fr)}\n.cl .n{font-weight:700}ul{margin:0 0 .9rem 3rem;padding-left:1.1rem}li{margin:0 0 .35rem}\nblockquote{margin:.6rem 0 1.1rem 3rem;padding:.2rem 0 .2rem 1rem;border-left:3px solid #C9C2B8;font-style:italic}\ntable{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;margin:.6rem 0 1.4rem;font-size:.92rem}th,td{text-align:left;vertical-align:top;border:1px solid #D8D1C7;padding:.55rem .65rem}\nthead th{background:#EFEBE5}tbody th{font-weight:700;width:34%}footer{margin-top:3rem;padding-top:1rem;border-top:1px solid #C9C2B8;color:#5E5A55;font-size:.85rem}\n@media (max-width:30rem){.cl{grid-template-columns:2.6rem minmax(0,1fr)}ul,blockquote{margin-left:2.6rem}h1{font-size:1.75rem}}\n@media print{body{background:#fff}main{padding:0}}\n</style></head>\n<body><main><article data-doc=\"PA-FAA-2026-11\">\n<p class=\"eyebrow\">PLOTART</p>\n<h1>Founding Artist Agreement</h1>\n<p class=\"sub\">Identifier PA-FAA-2026-11 · Text of 6 November 2026</p>\n<h2 id=\"1-parties-documents-and-acceptance\">1. Parties, documents and acceptance</h2>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c1.1\"><span class=\"n\">1.1</span><span>This agreement is between <strong>Colin MacAulay (registered as Colin Macaulay)</strong>, an individual trading as <strong>PlotNua</strong> under Business Name Registration No. 794392, who operates PlotArt as an initiative of PlotNua (“<strong>PlotArt</strong>”), and the artist who accepts it in PlotArt Studio (the “<strong>Artist</strong>”). PlotArt’s business address is shown on the Legal information page at plotnua.ie/terms.html. PlotArt’s contact email is hello@plotnua.ie.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c1.2\"><span class=\"n\">1.2</span><span>This agreement includes the <strong>PlotArt Gallery Publication and Image Licence, identifier PA-GPIL-2026-11</strong> (the “<strong>Licence</strong>”). If this agreement and the Licence differ, the term more favourable to the Artist applies.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c1.3\"><span class=\"n\">1.3</span><span>The Artist accepts this agreement and the Licence in PlotArt Studio by ticking the acceptance statement shown with this identified version. The agreement takes effect when PlotArt Studio records that acceptance. PlotArt confirms the acceptance in the Artist’s Studio account, where the Artist can download the exact version accepted at any time.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c1.4\"><span class=\"n\">1.4</span><span>For each acceptance PlotArt records: the agreement and Licence identifiers; a digital fingerprint of the exact text accepted; the date and time; the Studio account and email address used; the Artist’s professional name and, if the Artist chooses to give it, the Artist’s legal name; and the method of acceptance. These records are kept as described in clause 11.2.</span></p>\n<h2 id=\"2-the-founding-25\">2. The Founding 25</h2>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c2.1\"><span class=\"n\">2.1</span><span>The PlotArt Virtual Gallery is PlotArt’s online gallery of original art. The <strong>Founding 25</strong> are up to 25 artists, based or working on the island of Ireland, selected by PlotArt through a curated process to be among the first artists in it. The Virtual Gallery will grow beyond them.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c2.2\"><span class=\"n\">2.2</span><span>The Artist receives a dedicated online gallery and biography page in the Virtual Gallery. PlotArt sets the order in which galleries appear.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c2.3\"><span class=\"n\">2.3</span><span><strong>Collection.</strong> The Artist may display <strong>at least ten</strong> original artworks in the gallery at any one time. There is <strong>no minimum</strong>: a gallery may open with one artwork. The Artist may display more than ten. PlotArt may ask the Artist to keep the gallery to a reasonable size, or may decline a particular work, for reasonable technical or curatorial reasons, and will explain why. <strong>PlotArt will not remove artworks already published in the gallery in order to apply a limit, without the Artist’s agreement.</strong> Sold or withdrawn works may be replaced with other original works.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c2.4\"><span class=\"n\">2.4</span><span><strong>Founding year.</strong> The founding year lasts twelve months from the day the Artist’s gallery is first publicly published, not from the date of invitation, account creation or acceptance. It ends at the end of the day before the first anniversary of that date, Irish time. If the Artist accepts this agreement after first publication, the founding year still runs from first publication. PlotArt shows the start and end dates in PlotArt Studio.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c2.5\"><span class=\"n\">2.5</span><span><strong>Founding Artist designation.</strong> The Artist is a Founding Artist and keeps a permanent Founding 25 number. The Founding Artist badge is shown while the Artist’s gallery is active. If the gallery is removed, PlotArt keeps the historical record but names the Artist publicly as a Founding Artist only with the Artist’s agreement.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c2.6\"><span class=\"n\">2.6</span><span>Homepage features, promotional placement and other opportunities are at PlotArt’s discretion and are not guaranteed. PlotArt aims to rotate artist features fairly.</span></p>\n<h2 id=\"3-no-compulsory-fees-ever\">3. No compulsory fees, ever</h2>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c3.1\"><span class=\"n\">3.1</span><span>An “<strong>ordinary PlotArt artist gallery</strong>” is the standard online gallery and biography page that PlotArt provides to each artist it accepts into the Virtual Gallery, including the Artist’s gallery. <strong>Ordinary PlotArt artist galleries are never subject to compulsory membership, subscription or listing fees.</strong> PlotArt will never charge the Artist any such fee, during or after the founding year. This commitment binds anyone who takes over PlotArt.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c3.2\"><span class=\"n\">3.2</span><span>The only compulsory charge that PlotArt may ever introduce in connection with an ordinary PlotArt artist gallery is a <strong>commission on qualifying sales arising from enquiries introduced by PlotArt</strong>, and only under a separate commission agreement that the Artist expressly accepts (clause 6). <strong>No commission percentage has been decided.</strong></span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c3.3\"><span class=\"n\">3.3</span><span>PlotArt may offer optional additional services separately, on their own terms. They are <strong>never compulsory</strong>: the Artist’s gallery, its position, the Artist’s Founding Artist status and the enquiries PlotArt introduces never depend on taking up an optional service.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c3.4\"><span class=\"n\">3.4</span><span>During the founding year PlotArt charges <strong>no sales commission</strong> and no other charge of any kind.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c3.5\"><span class=\"n\">3.5</span><span>PlotArt does not ask for payment-card or bank details for the gallery. Nothing is payable to join, to remain or to leave.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c3.6\"><span class=\"n\">3.6</span><span>The Artist keeps the proceeds of every sale arranged directly with a buyer, subject only to the Artist’s own costs and obligations.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c3.7\"><span class=\"n\">3.7</span><span><strong>Continuity.</strong> The commitments in this clause 3 apply for as long as the Artist has a gallery on PlotArt. They are not a promise that PlotArt will operate indefinitely: PlotArt may close the Virtual Gallery for all artists under clause 10.2. The founding-year protections in clauses 2.4 and 10.2, and the protection of Founding Enquiries in clause 5, are not affected.</span></p>\n<h2 id=\"4-enquiries-and-sales\">4. Enquiries and sales</h2>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c4.1\"><span class=\"n\">4.1</span><span>PlotArt displays the Artist’s artwork and introduces potential buyers to the Artist, or to the Artist’s authorised representative, through PlotArt’s enquiry service or by email.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c4.2\"><span class=\"n\">4.2</span><span>Unless separately agreed in writing, PlotArt is not the seller, does not collect buyer payments, does not take ownership or possession of artworks, and does not arrange shipping or transit insurance.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c4.3\"><span class=\"n\">4.3</span><span>The Artist sets or confirms the sale price, contracts with the buyer, collects payment, arranges delivery and handles applicable consumer rights, returns, tax and other obligations of the sale.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c4.4\"><span class=\"n\">4.4</span><span>PlotArt does not guarantee enquiries or sales.</span></p>\n<h2 id=\"5-founding-enquiries-remain-commission-free-permanently\">5. Founding enquiries remain commission-free permanently</h2>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c5.1\"><span class=\"n\">5.1</span><span>A “<strong>Founding Enquiry</strong>” is any buyer enquiry that PlotArt introduces to the Artist during the founding year, by any route.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c5.2\"><span class=\"n\">5.2</span><span><strong>No PlotArt commission is ever payable on a sale arising from a Founding Enquiry</strong>, even if the sale completes after the founding year, and including later purchases by the same buyer that result from that same enquiry.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c5.3\"><span class=\"n\">5.3</span><span>The status of a Founding Enquiry is fixed on the date it is introduced. No later agreement, version or change of terms can impose commission on it.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c5.4\"><span class=\"n\">5.4</span><span><strong>Records.</strong> Enquiries that PlotArt introduces through its online enquiry service are recorded automatically with a reference, the introduction date and the artwork concerned. Enquiries that PlotArt introduces by email are recorded when PlotArt enters them in the enquiry log in PlotArt Studio; PlotArt does not guarantee that every enquiry introduced by email has been recorded. PlotArt makes the relevant records available to the Artist on reasonable request.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c5.5\"><span class=\"n\">5.5</span><span>PlotArt deletes a buyer’s name, email address and message 24 months after the enquiry, as set out in its privacy notice. It keeps the reference, the introduction date, the artwork and the Artist concerned, without the buyer’s contact details, for as long as this agreement lasts and six years afterwards, so that Founding Enquiries can be identified.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c5.6\"><span class=\"n\">5.6</span><span><strong>The commission-free status of a Founding Enquiry does not depend on PlotArt having recorded it, or keeping any record.</strong> If PlotArt cannot show that an enquiry was introduced after commission-bearing terms accepted by the Artist had taken effect, the enquiry is treated as a Founding Enquiry.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c5.7\"><span class=\"n\">5.7</span><span>The Artist is invited, but not required, to tell PlotArt about a sale resulting from a PlotArt enquiry within 14 days, identifying the work, the date and an approximate price band. There is no penalty for not doing so.</span></p>\n<h2 id=\"6-after-the-founding-year\">6. After the founding year</h2>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c6.1\"><span class=\"n\">6.1</span><span>PlotArt intends to fund the Virtual Gallery through a <strong>commission-only</strong> model: a commission on qualifying sales arising from enquiries introduced by PlotArt, as described in clause 3.2. <strong>No commission rate is agreed under this agreement.</strong></span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c6.2\"><span class=\"n\">6.2</span><span>The commitments in clauses 3.1 to 3.3 continue after the founding year.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c6.3\"><span class=\"n\">6.3</span><span>At least 60 days before the founding year ends, PlotArt will tell the Artist whether it proposes any commission arrangement and, if it does, will explain it.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c6.4\"><span class=\"n\">6.4</span><span>Commission may apply only to enquiries introduced <strong>after</strong> the Artist has expressly accepted a separate written commission agreement, identified by its own version, <strong>and</strong> that agreement has taken effect. Silence, continued use of PlotArt or the end of the founding year is not acceptance. <strong>PlotArt will not automatically convert the Artist to any commission-bearing arrangement.</strong></span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c6.5\"><span class=\"n\">6.5</span><span>If the Artist does not accept a commission agreement, the gallery may continue without charges on the existing basis until this agreement ends under clause 10.</span></p>\n<h2 id=\"7-artwork-accuracy-and-permissions\">7. Artwork, accuracy and permissions</h2>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c7.1\"><span class=\"n\">7.1</span><span>The Artist confirms that they own, or are authorised to offer, each listed work, and that they have the rights needed to provide its images and accompanying material.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c7.2\"><span class=\"n\">7.2</span><span>The Artist will supply accurate titles, medium, dimensions, year, price, framing and availability information, promptly correct inaccuracies, and mark a work as sold or withdrawn in PlotArt Studio, where that change takes effect straight away.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c7.3\"><span class=\"n\">7.3</span><span><strong>Original work and AI.</strong> PlotArt welcomes original digital work and AI-assisted practice. The Artist will disclose any meaningful use of AI in making a work. Images generated entirely from prompts are not automatically eligible as original artist-created artwork; PlotArt decides their eligibility.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c7.4\"><span class=\"n\">7.4</span><span>An Artist represented by another gallery or agent is responsible for obtaining any necessary consent and for avoiding conflicts with exclusivity arrangements.</span></p>\n<h2 id=\"8-copyright-and-image-licence\">8. Copyright and image licence</h2>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c8.1\"><span class=\"n\">8.1</span><span>Copyright, moral rights and ownership of the artworks, images and texts remain with the Artist or the respective rights holders. This agreement transfers no intellectual property to PlotArt.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c8.2\"><span class=\"n\">8.2</span><span>PlotArt uses the Artist’s images and information only as the Licence permits: non-exclusively and royalty-free, on PlotArt and PlotNua web pages. Any promotional use beyond those pages needs the Artist’s separate permission for each use.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c8.3\"><span class=\"n\">8.3</span><span>PlotArt will not sell or sublicense the Artist’s images, make products from them, add them to stock libraries, or use them to train artificial-intelligence models.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c8.4\"><span class=\"n\">8.4</span><span>When a work or the gallery is withdrawn, PlotArt removes the public listing within 14 days, subject to clause 6 of the Licence (lawful record retention, technical caches and material already distributed that cannot reasonably be recalled).</span></p>\n<h2 id=\"9-plotart-studio-and-publication\">9. PlotArt Studio and publication</h2>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c9.1\"><span class=\"n\">9.1</span><span>The Artist manages the gallery through <strong>PlotArt Studio</strong>, a private account signed in with a one-time code sent to the Artist’s email address. The Artist will keep access to that email address secure and will not share the sign-in. Changes the Artist submits in PlotArt Studio count as the Artist’s approval.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c9.2\"><span class=\"n\">9.2</span><span>PlotArt will not first publish the Artist’s gallery until the Artist has approved its preview by submitting it in PlotArt Studio.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c9.3\"><span class=\"n\">9.3</span><span>Later changes are published as follows. <strong>Straight away:</strong> availability (available, reserved, sold), withdrawing a work, and the order of works. <strong>After a quick check by PlotArt:</strong> prices and corrections to existing details. <strong>After review by PlotArt:</strong> new works, new or replacement photographs, the biography and the portrait.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c9.4\"><span class=\"n\">9.4</span><span>PlotArt may ask the Artist to correct, or may decline, a change that does not meet this agreement, the Licence or the photography guide, and will say why.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c9.5\"><span class=\"n\">9.5</span><span>PlotArt may make routine technical and presentation changes that do not materially misrepresent the artwork, as set out in clause 2.3 of the Licence.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c9.6\"><span class=\"n\">9.6</span><span>PlotArt may suspend Studio access to protect the Artist’s account or the gallery, and will tell the Artist why.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c9.7\"><span class=\"n\">9.7</span><span>Participation in the Mobile Gallery, the Living Gallery or any physical display requires a separate written arrangement covering custody, condition, transport, insurance, duration and responsibilities.</span></p>\n<h2 id=\"10-leaving-and-ending\">10. Leaving and ending</h2>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c10.1\"><span class=\"n\">10.1</span><span>The Artist may end this agreement at any time by telling PlotArt in PlotArt Studio or by email. PlotArt removes the public gallery within 14 days.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c10.2\"><span class=\"n\">10.2</span><span>PlotArt will not end this agreement during the founding year, except under clause 10.3 or if PlotArt closes the Virtual Gallery for all artists, in which case it gives at least 60 days’ written notice. After the founding year, PlotArt may end this agreement on at least 60 days’ written notice.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c10.3\"><span class=\"n\">10.3</span><span>PlotArt may promptly suspend or remove unlawful or materially infringing content, giving an explanation where appropriate. PlotArt may end this agreement for a serious or repeated breach after giving the Artist a reasonable opportunity to put it right.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c10.4\"><span class=\"n\">10.4</span><span>Ending this agreement, or PlotArt closing the Virtual Gallery, does not affect the permanent commission-free status of Founding Enquiries (clause 5), obligations already owed to buyers, or any other term intended to continue.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c10.5\"><span class=\"n\">10.5</span><span>Neither party owes any fee for ending this agreement.</span></p>\n<h2 id=\"11-information-and-communications\">11. Information and communications</h2>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c11.1\"><span class=\"n\">11.1</span><span>PlotArt processes artist and enquiry information in accordance with its privacy notice at plotnua.ie/privacy.html and its data-protection obligations.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c11.2\"><span class=\"n\">11.2</span><span>PlotArt keeps the acceptance records described in clause 1.4 for as long as this agreement lasts and for six years afterwards, so that what was agreed can be shown, and then deletes them unless the law requires otherwise. Earlier acceptances are never altered or re-attributed to later wording.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c11.3\"><span class=\"n\">11.3</span><span>Notices are given by email: to the address the Artist uses for PlotArt Studio, and to hello@plotnua.ie. Each party will promptly tell the other of a change to its contact details.</span></p>\n<h2 id=\"12-responsibility-and-governing-law\">12. Responsibility and governing law</h2>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c12.1\"><span class=\"n\">12.1</span><span>Each party remains responsible for its own acts and obligations.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c12.2\"><span class=\"n\">12.2</span><span>Nothing in this agreement excludes or limits any liability that cannot lawfully be excluded or limited, or affects statutory consumer rights.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c12.3\"><span class=\"n\">12.3</span><span>This agreement is governed by the law of Ireland, and the courts of Ireland have jurisdiction. This does not take away any protection the Artist has under mandatory law where the Artist lives.</span></p>\n<h2 id=\"13-changes-to-this-agreement\">13. Changes to this agreement</h2>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c13.1\"><span class=\"n\">13.1</span><span>PlotArt may propose changes as a new, identified version in PlotArt Studio. A new version applies to the Artist only when the Artist expressly accepts it there.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c13.2\"><span class=\"n\">13.2</span><span>No change may retrospectively alter the protection of Founding Enquiries, introduce any compulsory fee, or introduce commission, without the Artist’s express acceptance under clause 6.4. Every version the Artist has accepted remains on record and can be downloaded.</span></p>\n<h2 id=\"14-general\">14. General</h2>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c14.1\"><span class=\"n\">14.1</span><span>This agreement and the Licence together form the whole agreement between PlotArt and the Artist about the Founding 25.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c14.2\"><span class=\"n\">14.2</span><span>This agreement does not create a partnership, employment or agency. Neither party can bind the other.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c14.3\"><span class=\"n\">14.3</span><span>PlotArt may transfer this agreement only to a business that takes over PlotArt, on the same terms, including clauses 3 and 5, and will tell the Artist by email.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c14.4\"><span class=\"n\">14.4</span><span>If any part of this agreement is found unenforceable, the rest continues to apply.</span></p>\n<h2 id=\"acceptance-in-plotart-studio\">Acceptance in PlotArt Studio</h2>\n<p>The Artist accepts by ticking the following statement in PlotArt Studio:</p>\n<blockquote>“I have read and accept the PlotArt Founding Artist Agreement PA-FAA-2026-11, including the Gallery Publication and Image Licence PA-GPIL-2026-11.”</blockquote>\n<p>PlotArt Studio then records, and shows in the Artist’s account:</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Record</th><th scope=\"col\">Completed by PlotArt Studio</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope=\"row\">Agreement and Licence</th><td>PA-FAA-2026-11 and PA-GPIL-2026-11, with the fingerprint of each exact text</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Artist</th><td>Professional name; legal name, optional (entered by the Artist at acceptance if they wish); Studio account email</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">PlotArt</th><td>Colin MacAulay (registered as Colin Macaulay), trading as PlotNua, Business Name Registration No. 794392</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Accepted</th><td>Date and time (Irish time), and method: PlotArt Studio electronic acceptance</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Founding year</th><td>First-publication date, and the founding year’s end date (clause 2.4)</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</article>\n<footer>PlotArt Founding Artist Agreement  ·  PA-FAA-2026-11 · plotnua.ie · hello@plotnua.ie</footer></main></body></html>\n","pdf_b64":"","html_sha256":"62adedbf330a0f6d02e952c7f4f7bfc9232696103dd10d52fa72b99a88693463","pdf_sha256":"cc3294340834db30c14c47cb811042d91e3619e73aca3dfd2fafc032d8bd8011"},"PA-GPIL-2026-11":{"title":"PlotArt Gallery Publication and Image Licence","html":"<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en-IE\"><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n<title>PlotArt Gallery Publication and Image Licence · PA-GPIL-2026-11</title><meta name=\"robots\" content=\"noindex, nofollow\">\n<style>\n:root{color-scheme:light}body{margin:0;background:#F4F1EC;color:#1B1C1E;font:16px/1.6 Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif}\nmain{max-width:46rem;margin:0 auto;padding:2.5rem 1rem 4rem}.eyebrow{margin:0;color:#AE6245;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.18em;font-size:.8rem}\nh1{font:400 2.1rem/1.15 Georgia,serif;margin:.3rem 0 .4rem}.sub{margin:0 0 2rem;color:#5E5A55;font-size:.95rem}\nh2{font:400 1.3rem/1.3 Georgia,serif;margin:2.2rem 0 .7rem}p{margin:0 0 .8rem}.cl{display:grid;grid-template-columns:3rem minmax(0,1fr)}\n.cl .n{font-weight:700}ul{margin:0 0 .9rem 3rem;padding-left:1.1rem}li{margin:0 0 .35rem}\nblockquote{margin:.6rem 0 1.1rem 3rem;padding:.2rem 0 .2rem 1rem;border-left:3px solid #C9C2B8;font-style:italic}\ntable{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;margin:.6rem 0 1.4rem;font-size:.92rem}th,td{text-align:left;vertical-align:top;border:1px solid #D8D1C7;padding:.55rem .65rem}\nthead th{background:#EFEBE5}tbody th{font-weight:700;width:34%}footer{margin-top:3rem;padding-top:1rem;border-top:1px solid #C9C2B8;color:#5E5A55;font-size:.85rem}\n@media (max-width:30rem){.cl{grid-template-columns:2.6rem minmax(0,1fr)}ul,blockquote{margin-left:2.6rem}h1{font-size:1.75rem}}\n@media print{body{background:#fff}main{padding:0}}\n</style></head>\n<body><main><article data-doc=\"PA-GPIL-2026-11\">\n<p class=\"eyebrow\">PLOTART</p>\n<h1>Gallery Publication and Image Licence</h1>\n<p class=\"sub\">Identifier PA-GPIL-2026-11 · Text of 6 November 2026</p>\n<h2 id=\"1-who-this-licence-is-between-and-what-it-covers\">1. Who this licence is between, and what it covers</h2>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c1.1\"><span class=\"n\">1.1</span><span>This licence is between <strong>Colin MacAulay (registered as Colin Macaulay)</strong>, an individual trading as <strong>PlotNua</strong> under Business Name Registration No. 794392, who operates PlotArt as an initiative of PlotNua (“<strong>PlotArt</strong>”), and the artist who accepts it in PlotArt Studio (“<strong>you</strong>”).</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c1.2\"><span class=\"n\">1.2</span><span>It applies to every artist with a PlotArt gallery. For a Founding Artist it forms part of the PlotArt Founding Artist Agreement PA-FAA-2026-11.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c1.3\"><span class=\"n\">1.3</span><span>It covers what PlotArt may publish about you and your work, and how: your gallery; your biography; your portrait, if you supply one; your artworks’ images and details; and any room views made from them.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c1.4\"><span class=\"n\">1.4</span><span><strong>You keep ownership and copyright</strong> of your works, images and words, and your moral rights. This licence lets PlotArt use them only as set out here.</span></p>\n<h2 id=\"2-approval-comes-first\">2. Approval comes first</h2>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c2.1\"><span class=\"n\">2.1</span><span>PlotArt publishes nothing until you have approved a preview of exactly what will appear, by submitting it in PlotArt Studio.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c2.2\"><span class=\"n\">2.2</span><span>Changes you make in PlotArt Studio count as your approval. They are published straight away, after a quick check, or after review, as your artist agreement sets out (for Founding Artists, clause 9.3 of PA-FAA-2026-11).</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c2.3\"><span class=\"n\">2.3</span><span>PlotArt may make purely technical changes without asking: resizing, compressing, converting file formats, converting colours to the standard web colour space (sRGB), removing hidden file information such as camera details and location data, and making thumbnails <strong>without cropping into the artwork</strong>. PlotArt will never otherwise alter the artwork’s appearance, colour balance or content.</span></p>\n<h2 id=\"3-the-licence\">3. The licence</h2>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c3.1\"><span class=\"n\">3.1</span><span>You grant PlotArt a <strong>non-exclusive, royalty-free licence</strong>, for as long as your gallery is listed (and, after removal, only as clause 6 allows), to reproduce, display and make available the content you have approved:</span></p>\n<ul><li><strong>on PlotArt and PlotNua web pages:</strong> your gallery, your artwork pages, the Virtual Gallery, and PlotArt pages that feature artists in fair rotation;</li><li><strong>as room views</strong>, if any are made: digital illustrations showing an image of your work at its true proportions in a room setting. Each is made only from images you supply or approve, is labelled as an illustration, and is shown to you before publication;</li><li><strong>as thumbnails and link previews</strong> that show your work in search results and when a PlotArt page is shared.</li></ul>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c3.2\"><span class=\"n\">3.2</span><span><strong>Promotional use beyond the website needs your separate yes for each use</strong>: social media posts, newsletters, press, print, advertising or partner features. There is no standing opt-in. You can say no without any effect on your gallery.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c3.3\"><span class=\"n\">3.3</span><span>PlotArt will not sell, license or give your images to anyone else; make prints or products from them; add your work to stock libraries; or use your images to train or develop artificial-intelligence models, or allow others to do so, so far as this is within PlotArt’s control.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c3.4\"><span class=\"n\">3.4</span><span>PlotArt credits you as the artist wherever your work appears on PlotArt. Credit in link previews depends on the platform.</span></p>\n<h2 id=\"4-your-permissions-and-declarations\">4. Your permissions and declarations</h2>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c4.1\"><span class=\"n\">4.1</span><span>You confirm that you have the right to grant this licence for every image and text you supply. For each photograph you upload, you will say whether you took it or another photographer took it with their permission, giving their name for the credit. For works shown with other people’s property or likeness, you have any permission needed.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c4.2\"><span class=\"n\">4.2</span><span>If a gallery or agent represents you, you confirm that they agree to this licence.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c4.3\"><span class=\"n\">4.3</span><span>For each work you will say whether AI played a meaningful part in making it. Where it did, a short disclosure is shown on the work’s page.</span></p>\n<h2 id=\"5-your-choices-about-personal-details\">5. Your choices about personal details</h2>\n<table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Item</th><th scope=\"col\">Shown publicly?</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope=\"row\">Your name (the name you work under)</th><td>Yes: it is your gallery</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Biography and statement (your own words)</th><td>Yes, as you approve them</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">County</th><td>Only if you choose. You can withdraw this at any time</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Portrait photograph</th><td>Only if you supply one and choose to show it. You can withdraw this at any time</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Email address or phone number</th><td>Never published. Buyers reach you through PlotArt’s enquiry service; they see your email address only if you reply to them by email</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<h2 id=\"6-changing-your-mind-removal-and-deletion\">6. Changing your mind, removal and deletion</h2>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c6.1\"><span class=\"n\">6.1</span><span>You can withdraw any work, image or detail, or your whole gallery, at any time in PlotArt Studio or by emailing hello@plotnua.ie. PlotArt removes it from its public website within 14 days, and usually much sooner.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c6.2\"><span class=\"n\">6.2</span><span>Withdrawing your choice to show your county or portrait takes effect within the same period.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c6.3\"><span class=\"n\">6.3</span><span><strong>Originals.</strong> PlotArt keeps your original photographs privately in PlotArt Studio to prepare the web versions. A work you withdraw from your gallery stays in your private Studio account, with its photographs, so that you can show it again, until you delete it.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c6.4\"><span class=\"n\">6.4</span><span><strong>Deleting.</strong> When you delete a photograph, delete a work that is not on show, or replace your portrait in PlotArt Studio, PlotArt deletes the original and its private copies within 30 days. If the photograph is still shown in your published gallery at that point, for example while its replacement is being reviewed, PlotArt deletes it within 30 days after it stops being shown.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c6.5\"><span class=\"n\">6.5</span><span><strong>Leaving.</strong> If you leave PlotArt, PlotArt keeps your account, gallery records and original photographs for 12 months after you stop taking part, as its privacy notice explains, and then deletes them. You can ask PlotArt to delete your original photographs sooner by emailing hello@plotnua.ie.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c6.6\"><span class=\"n\">6.6</span><span><strong>Records PlotArt keeps.</strong> PlotArt keeps a record of what was published and when, without images. The web versions of published images also remain in PlotArt’s private version history of its website, which is not public and is not used for any other purpose. PlotArt may also keep anything the law requires, or that it needs to establish, exercise or defend a legal claim.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c6.7\"><span class=\"n\">6.7</span><span>After your gallery is removed, PlotArt names you publicly as a Founding Artist only with your agreement.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c6.8\"><span class=\"n\">6.8</span><span>PlotArt cannot control copies that others have already made, such as search-engine caches, screenshots or shares. It will ask search engines to refresh where it reasonably can.</span></p>\n<h2 id=\"7-general\">7. General</h2>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c7.1\"><span class=\"n\">7.1</span><span>This licence is read with your PlotArt artist agreement (for Founding Artists, PA-FAA-2026-11). That agreement’s clauses on responsibility, governing law, changes and notices apply to this licence.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c7.2\"><span class=\"n\">7.2</span><span>PlotArt will not change this licence to widen how your content is used unless you accept a new, identified version in PlotArt Studio.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c7.3\"><span class=\"n\">7.3</span><span>This version applies from the date you accept it. It does not change any earlier acceptance, and no earlier acceptance is treated as acceptance of this wording.</span></p>\n<h2 id=\"acceptance-in-plotart-studio\">Acceptance in PlotArt Studio</h2>\n<p>Founding Artists accept this licence together with the Founding Artist Agreement, in one statement:</p>\n<blockquote>“I have read and accept the PlotArt Founding Artist Agreement PA-FAA-2026-11, including the Gallery Publication and Image Licence PA-GPIL-2026-11.”</blockquote>\n<p>PlotArt Studio records the licence identifier, the fingerprint of this exact text, the date and time, your Studio account and the method of acceptance, and keeps this version available for you to download.</p>\n</article>\n<footer>PlotArt Gallery Publication and Image Licence  ·  PA-GPIL-2026-11 · plotnua.ie · hello@plotnua.ie</footer></main></body></html>\n","pdf_b64":"","html_sha256":"f4a2c72e8068a267afac87a7555ac509fb64d9b9a9385f389a855d5ba8408f92","pdf_sha256":"aa3c27423f21877006bac7bd5e3132111dea5e2914617cf30826b4203637ba17"},"PA-GAA-2026-11":{"title":"PlotArt Gallery Artist Agreement","html":"<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en-IE\"><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n<title>PlotArt Gallery Artist Agreement · PA-GAA-2026-11</title><meta name=\"robots\" content=\"noindex, nofollow\">\n<style>\n:root{color-scheme:light}body{margin:0;background:#F4F1EC;color:#1B1C1E;font:16px/1.6 Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif}\nmain{max-width:46rem;margin:0 auto;padding:2.5rem 1rem 4rem}.eyebrow{margin:0;color:#AE6245;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.18em;font-size:.8rem}\nh1{font:400 2.1rem/1.15 Georgia,serif;margin:.3rem 0 .4rem}.sub{margin:0 0 2rem;color:#5E5A55;font-size:.95rem}\nh2{font:400 1.3rem/1.3 Georgia,serif;margin:2.2rem 0 .7rem}p{margin:0 0 .8rem}.cl{display:grid;grid-template-columns:3rem minmax(0,1fr)}\n.cl .n{font-weight:700}ul{margin:0 0 .9rem 3rem;padding-left:1.1rem}li{margin:0 0 .35rem}\nblockquote{margin:.6rem 0 1.1rem 3rem;padding:.2rem 0 .2rem 1rem;border-left:3px solid #C9C2B8;font-style:italic}\ntable{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;margin:.6rem 0 1.4rem;font-size:.92rem}th,td{text-align:left;vertical-align:top;border:1px solid #D8D1C7;padding:.55rem .65rem}\nthead th{background:#EFEBE5}tbody th{font-weight:700;width:34%}footer{margin-top:3rem;padding-top:1rem;border-top:1px solid #C9C2B8;color:#5E5A55;font-size:.85rem}\n@media (max-width:30rem){.cl{grid-template-columns:2.6rem minmax(0,1fr)}ul,blockquote{margin-left:2.6rem}h1{font-size:1.75rem}}\n@media print{body{background:#fff}main{padding:0}}\n</style></head>\n<body><main><article data-doc=\"PA-GAA-2026-11\">\n<p class=\"eyebrow\">PLOTART</p>\n<h1>Gallery Artist Agreement</h1>\n<p class=\"sub\">Identifier PA-GAA-2026-11 · Text of 13 November 2026</p>\n<h2 id=\"1-parties-documents-and-acceptance\">1. Parties, documents and acceptance</h2>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c1.1\"><span class=\"n\">1.1</span><span>This agreement is between Colin MacAulay (registered as Colin Macaulay), an individual trading as PlotNua under Business Name Registration No. 794392, who operates PlotArt as an initiative of PlotNua (“<strong>PlotArt</strong>”), and the artist who accepts it in PlotArt Studio (the “<strong>Artist</strong>”). PlotArt’s business address is shown on the Legal information page at plotnua.ie/terms.html. PlotArt’s contact email is hello@plotnua.ie.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c1.2\"><span class=\"n\">1.2</span><span>This agreement includes the PlotArt Gallery Publication and Image Licence, identifier PA-GPIL-2026-11 (the “<strong>Licence</strong>”). If this agreement and the Licence differ, the term more favourable to the Artist applies, except as clause 18.3 explains for commission records.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c1.3\"><span class=\"n\">1.3</span><span>The Artist accepts this agreement and the Licence in PlotArt Studio by ticking the acceptance statement shown with this identified version. The agreement takes effect when PlotArt Studio records that acceptance. The Artist can download the exact version accepted at any time.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c1.4\"><span class=\"n\">1.4</span><span>For each acceptance PlotArt records: the agreement and Licence identifiers; a digital fingerprint of the exact text accepted; the date and time; the Studio account and email address used; the Artist’s professional name and, if the Artist chooses to give it, the Artist’s legal name; and the method of acceptance.</span></p>\n<h2 id=\"2-the-gallery\">2. The gallery</h2>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c2.1\"><span class=\"n\">2.1</span><span>PlotArt is an independently curated online gallery of contemporary Irish art. The Artist has been selected by PlotArt and receives a dedicated online gallery and biography page in the PlotArt <strong>Artists’ Gallery</strong>, the online gallery the Licence calls the Virtual Gallery. PlotArt sets the order in which galleries appear by hand, for curatorial reasons. The order is not influenced by any fee, payment, commission rate or individual variation.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c2.2\"><span class=\"n\">2.2</span><span>The Artist may start with one artwork and add more over time. PlotArt may ask the Artist to keep the gallery to a reasonable size, or may decline a particular work, for reasonable technical or curatorial reasons, and will explain why. PlotArt will not remove published artworks to apply a limit without the Artist’s agreement.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c2.3\"><span class=\"n\">2.3</span><span><strong>Founding Artists.</strong> This agreement is for artists who join PlotArt under its standard commission-based terms. It does not apply to an artist who holds the PlotArt Founding Artist Agreement (PA-FAA-2026-11) unless that artist separately and expressly accepts it, as clause 6.4 of that agreement requires. Nothing in this agreement changes a Founding Artist’s agreement, founding year, the commission-free status of Founding Enquiries, or any notice that agreement requires.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c2.4\"><span class=\"n\">2.4</span><span>Homepage features, promotional placement and other opportunities are at PlotArt’s discretion and are not guaranteed.</span></p>\n<h2 id=\"3-no-fees\">3. No fees</h2>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c3.1\"><span class=\"n\">3.1</span><span>For as long as this agreement applies to the Artist, PlotArt charges the Artist no upfront, joining, membership, subscription or listing fee for the Artist’s gallery.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c3.2\"><span class=\"n\">3.2</span><span>The only charge under this agreement is PlotArt’s commission on Qualifying Sales (clause 5). PlotArt does not ask for payment-card or bank details to join, remain or leave.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c3.3\"><span class=\"n\">3.3</span><span>PlotArt may offer different commercial arrangements to other artists, or propose a new version of this agreement under clause 20. A new version, or any fee, applies to the Artist only if the Artist expressly accepts it. Until then this agreement, including clause 3.1, continues to apply.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c3.4\"><span class=\"n\">3.4</span><span>PlotArt may offer optional additional services separately, on their own terms. The Artist’s gallery, its position and the enquiries PlotArt introduces never depend on taking one up.</span></p>\n<h2 id=\"4-enquiries-sales-and-no-exclusivity\">4. Enquiries, sales and no exclusivity</h2>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c4.1\"><span class=\"n\">4.1</span><span>PlotArt displays the Artist’s artwork and introduces potential collectors to the Artist, or to the Artist’s authorised representative, through PlotArt’s enquiry service or by email.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c4.2\"><span class=\"n\">4.2</span><span><strong>Collectors pay the Artist directly.</strong> PlotArt is not the seller. It does not collect collector payments, take ownership or possession of artworks, or arrange shipping, insurance or handling. The Artist sets or confirms the price, contracts with the collector, collects payment, arranges delivery, and handles applicable consumer rights, returns, tax and other obligations of the sale.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c4.3\"><span class=\"n\">4.3</span><span><strong>Shipping, insurance and handling</strong> are arranged and paid between the Artist and the collector. Amounts the collector pays for them are not part of the Commission Base (clause 5.6).</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c4.4\"><span class=\"n\">4.4</span><span><strong>No exclusivity.</strong> The Artist may sell their work anywhere, show with other galleries and be represented by others. PlotArt asks for no exclusivity of any kind.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c4.5\"><span class=\"n\">4.5</span><span>PlotArt does not guarantee enquiries or sales.</span></p>\n<h2 id=\"5-commission\">5. Commission</h2>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c5.1\"><span class=\"n\">5.1</span><span><strong>Rate.</strong> PlotArt’s commission on a Qualifying Sale is 15% of the Commission Base, less any PlotArt-Funded Discount (clause 6) (the “<strong>Full Commission</strong>”). The Artist keeps at least 85% of the Commission Base.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c5.2\"><span class=\"n\">5.2</span><span><strong>VAT.</strong> The 15% commission includes any VAT that applies to it. The Artist pays no more than 15% of the Commission Base in total. If PlotArt is registered for VAT, its invoice shows the VAT included within the 15%.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c5.3\"><span class=\"n\">5.3</span><span><strong>Qualifying Introduction.</strong> A Qualifying Introduction is a collector introduced to the Artist by PlotArt on or after the date this agreement takes effect, by any of these routes:</span></p>\n<ul><li>(a) an enquiry sent through PlotArt’s enquiry service, which carries a PlotArt reference;</li><li>(b) an enquiry PlotArt passes to the Artist by email and records with a PlotArt reference; or</li><li>(c) a collector who contacts the Artist directly and tells the Artist, before the sale is agreed, that they found the Artist through PlotArt (a “<strong>Direct Approach</strong>”).</li></ul>\n<p>A collector the Artist already knew before that date is not a Qualifying Introduction (clause 7).</p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c5.4\"><span class=\"n\">5.4</span><span><strong>Introduction Date.</strong> The Introduction Date is the date PlotArt introduced the collector, as shown by its reference, or, for a Direct Approach, the date the collector told the Artist they found the Artist through PlotArt. If PlotArt introduces the same collector again, a new Introduction Date applies only if the earlier Attribution Period has ended; a further enquiry during a running period does not extend it.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c5.5\"><span class=\"n\">5.5</span><span><strong>Qualifying Sale and the Attribution Period.</strong> A Qualifying Sale is a sale of any Original Artwork by the Artist, whether or not it is shown on PlotArt, to a collector from a Qualifying Introduction (or to someone buying on that collector’s behalf) where either:</span></p>\n<ul><li>(a) the sale is agreed within <strong>24 months</strong> of the Introduction Date, a period that ends at the end of the day before the second anniversary of the Introduction Date, Irish time (the “<strong>Attribution Period</strong>”); or</li><li>(b) the sale is agreed after the Attribution Period but results from <strong>Documented Negotiations</strong> that began within it.</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Documented Negotiations</strong> are written exchanges between the Artist (or the Artist’s representative) and the collector about the purchase of a particular, identified artwork. Under (b), only the sale of that artwork, resulting from those negotiations, is a Qualifying Sale. Any other later purchase by the same collector is not.</p>\n<p><strong>Original Artwork</strong> means an original work made by the Artist, together with any frame or mount sold with it, and a signed, limited-edition fine-art print of the Artist’s work. It does not include open-edition reproductions or merchandise (for example posters, cards or products bearing images of the Artist’s work).</p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c5.6\"><span class=\"n\">5.6</span><span><strong>Commission Base.</strong> The Commission Base is the price agreed between the Artist and the collector for the artwork itself, before any PlotArt-Funded Discount. It includes any frame or mount sold with the artwork. It excludes shipping, insurance, handling, installation and any VAT the Artist charges on the sale. For a sale through a representing gallery or agent, the Commission Base is set by clause 12.2.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c5.7\"><span class=\"n\">5.7</span><span><strong>No commission</strong> is payable on:</span></p>\n<ul><li>(a) an Independent Sale (clause 7);</li><li>(b) a sale that is not a Qualifying Sale under clause 5.5, including any sale agreed after the Attribution Period that does not result from Documented Negotiations begun within it;</li><li>(c) a sale that is cancelled, or fully refunded, before or after payment (clause 9);</li><li>(d) an enquiry, viewing or conversation that does not result in a completed sale; or</li><li>(e) newly commissioned artwork, including a commission agreed after a collector uses the “Enquire about a commission” option on the Artist’s gallery, unless PlotArt and the Artist have separately agreed commission terms for it in writing.</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Newly commissioned artwork</strong> is a work the collector asks the Artist to create, to the collector’s request (for example its subject, size or setting), that did not exist and was not in progress when the commission was agreed. A work the Artist made independently, including one finished after the Introduction Date, is not newly commissioned, and minor changes to an existing work (such as reframing) do not make it so. If a collector introduced through the “Enquire about a commission” option buys an existing work, that sale is treated like any other sale.</p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c5.8\"><span class=\"n\">5.8</span><span>Commission is due only on a <strong>completed</strong> sale: when the Artist has received payment for the artwork, or an instalment of it (clause 10).</span></p>\n<h2 id=\"6-optional-collector-discount-funded-by-plotart\">6. Optional collector discount funded by PlotArt</h2>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c6.1\"><span class=\"n\">6.1</span><span>PlotArt may, at its discretion, offer a particular collector a discount of up to <strong>5% of the Commission Base</strong> (a “<strong>PlotArt-Funded Discount</strong>”), but <strong>only if the Artist agrees</strong> to that discount for that sale, in writing (including by email or in PlotArt Studio), before it is offered. PlotArt decides whether to propose a discount; the Artist decides whether to agree.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c6.2\"><span class=\"n\">6.2</span><span>A PlotArt-Funded Discount is paid for entirely out of PlotArt’s commission. The collector pays the Artist the Commission Base less the discount, and PlotArt’s commission is reduced by the same amount, so the Artist still keeps 85% of the Commission Base.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c6.3\"><span class=\"n\">6.3</span><span>Example (illustration only). Commission Base €1,000.</span></p>\n<ul><li><strong>No discount:</strong> the collector pays the Artist €1,000. PlotArt invoices €150. The Artist keeps €850.</li><li><strong>With a 5% PlotArt-Funded Discount:</strong> the collector pays the Artist €950. PlotArt invoices €100. The Artist keeps €850.</li></ul>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c6.4\"><span class=\"n\">6.4</span><span>The Artist is not obliged to accept a PlotArt-Funded Discount, and refusing one never affects the Artist’s gallery or the introductions PlotArt makes. PlotArt does not advertise PlotArt-Funded Discounts publicly; they are offered only to individual collectors.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c6.5\"><span class=\"n\">6.5</span><span>No PlotArt-Funded Discount can be offered on a sale that carries no commission, or on a sale through a representing gallery or agent (clause 12.2).</span></p>\n<h2 id=\"7-independent-sales\">7. Independent sales</h2>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c7.1\"><span class=\"n\">7.1</span><span>An <strong>Independent Sale</strong> is a sale to a collector who did not come from a Qualifying Introduction. That includes a collector who:</span></p>\n<ul><li>(a) bought from, commissioned, or was in documented contact with the Artist before the Introduction Date, other than through an earlier Qualifying Introduction;</li><li>(b) found the Artist through the Artist’s own channels, another gallery, an exhibition or any other source, without a PlotArt introduction; or</li><li>(c) is otherwise shown, on reasonable evidence, to have reached the Artist independently.</li></ul>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c7.2\"><span class=\"n\">7.2</span><span>If PlotArt and the Artist disagree about whether a sale is independent, the Artist may give PlotArt reasonable evidence (for example earlier correspondence or a previous sale record). Both will act in good faith. If, once reasonable evidence has been considered, the origin of the collector remains genuinely uncertain, the sale is treated as an Independent Sale.</span></p>\n<h2 id=\"8-sale-reporting-invoices-and-payment\">8. Sale reporting, invoices and payment</h2>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c8.1\"><span class=\"n\">8.1</span><span><strong>Reporting.</strong> The Artist will report each Qualifying Sale to PlotArt within <strong>14 days</strong> of receiving payment, in PlotArt Studio (or by email to hello@plotnua.ie until Studio offers this). The report gives:</span></p>\n<ul><li>the PlotArt reference, or, for a Direct Approach, the date the collector mentioned PlotArt;</li><li>the artwork;</li><li>the date the sale was agreed (and, if clause 5.5(b) applies, the date the Documented Negotiations began);</li><li>the amount the collector was due to pay for the artwork, and any PlotArt-Funded Discount; and</li><li>whether further instalments are due.</li></ul>\n<p>It includes no collector contact details.</p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c8.2\"><span class=\"n\">8.2</span><span><strong>Direct Approaches.</strong> The Artist reports a sale to a collector who told the Artist, before the sale was agreed, that they found the Artist through PlotArt. The Artist is not required to ask collectors how they found the Artist, or to investigate the source of any enquiry.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c8.3\"><span class=\"n\">8.3</span><span><strong>Invoices.</strong> PlotArt issues an invoice for its commission after the report, normally monthly. Each invoice identifies the sale by its PlotArt reference (or date of Direct Approach) and artwork, and shows how the commission was calculated.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c8.4\"><span class=\"n\">8.4</span><span><strong>Payment.</strong> The Artist pays each invoice by bank transfer within <strong>30 days</strong> of the invoice date. PlotArt charges no fees or interest for late payment beyond any that the law itself provides. Reminders, suspension and ending for unpaid commission are covered in clauses 17.3 and 17.4.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c8.5\"><span class=\"n\">8.5</span><span><strong>Currency.</strong> Commission is calculated and invoiced in euro. A sale in another currency is converted at the European Central Bank reference rate on the date the Artist received payment.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c8.6\"><span class=\"n\">8.6</span><span><strong>Corrections.</strong> If either party finds an error in a report or invoice, it tells the other promptly. An overpayment is refunded, and an underpayment is invoiced, within 30 days. PlotArt keeps the records of introductions, reports and invoices (clause 18.3); the Artist is not required to keep any record for PlotArt beyond what it needs to make an accurate report.</span></p>\n<h2 id=\"9-cancellations-refunds-and-returns\">9. Cancellations, refunds and returns</h2>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c9.1\"><span class=\"n\">9.1</span><span>No commission is payable on a sale that is cancelled or fully refunded. If PlotArt has already been paid, it refunds the commission within 30 days of the Artist telling it, with reasonable evidence.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c9.2\"><span class=\"n\">9.2</span><span><strong>Partial refunds.</strong> If the collector receives a partial refund, the commission due is the Full Commission multiplied by the amount the Artist keeps for the artwork, divided by the amount the collector was due to pay for the artwork. PlotArt credits or refunds any difference within 30 days.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c9.3\"><span class=\"n\">9.3</span><span>Handling a cancellation, return or refund is a matter between the Artist and the collector, under the law that applies to their sale.</span></p>\n<h2 id=\"10-instalments\">10. Instalments</h2>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c10.1\"><span class=\"n\">10.1</span><span>If the collector pays in instalments, each instalment carries the same share of the Full Commission as the instalment bears to the total the collector is due to pay for the artwork. Commission on each instalment is due once it is received, and each instalment is reported under clause 8.1.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c10.2\"><span class=\"n\">10.2</span><span>If an instalment sale is later cancelled, commission is due only on the instalments the Artist keeps, calculated under clause 10.1.</span></p>\n<h2 id=\"11-artwork-removed-from-plotart-and-after-this-agreement-ends\">11. Artwork removed from PlotArt, and after this agreement ends</h2>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c11.1\"><span class=\"n\">11.1</span><span>Withdrawing an artwork from the gallery does not affect commission on its sale if the sale is a Qualifying Sale under clause 5.5.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c11.2\"><span class=\"n\">11.2</span><span>When this agreement ends, for any reason, commission remains payable on Qualifying Sales to collectors whose Introduction Date fell before the end, where the sale is agreed within the Attribution Period or under clause 5.5(b). No commission arises from collectors first introduced after the agreement ends.</span></p>\n<h2 id=\"12-existing-gallery-representation-and-third-party-sales\">12. Existing gallery representation and third-party sales</h2>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c12.1\"><span class=\"n\">12.1</span><span>An Artist represented by another gallery or agent is responsible for obtaining any consent needed to show work on PlotArt, and for avoiding conflicts with any exclusivity they have agreed with others.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c12.2\"><span class=\"n\">12.2</span><span><strong>Sales through a representing gallery or agent.</strong> A “<strong>representing gallery or agent</strong>” is a gallery or agent that represents the Artist under an arrangement made independently of PlotArt and before the Introduction Date, and that takes a commission on the sale. If a collector from a Qualifying Introduction buys the Artist’s work through a representing gallery or agent, and the sale is a Qualifying Sale under clause 5.5, the Commission Base is the amount the Artist receives from the gallery or agent for the artwork. PlotArt’s commission is 15% of that amount, not 15% of the full price the collector pays.</span></p>\n<p>Example (illustration only). The collector pays €1,000. The representing gallery keeps 40% (€400), and the Artist receives €600. PlotArt’s commission is €90, and the Artist keeps €510.</p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c12.3\"><span class=\"n\">12.3</span><span>The Artist reports such a sale under clause 8.1, giving the amount the Artist received. A statement from the Artist of the amount received is enough. PlotArt may ask for reasonable confirmation (such as the gallery’s remittance) only if there is a genuine doubt. PlotArt does not need to see the gallery’s own agreement.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c12.4\"><span class=\"n\">12.4</span><span>If the representing gallery or agent itself introduced the collector to the Artist’s work before the Introduction Date, the sale is an Independent Sale.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c12.5\"><span class=\"n\">12.5</span><span>A sale by another gallery to its own collector, without a Qualifying Introduction, is an Independent Sale.</span></p>\n<h2 id=\"13-individual-variations\">13. Individual variations</h2>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c13.1\"><span class=\"n\">13.1</span><span>PlotArt and the Artist may agree different commercial terms for the Artist, for example a different rate, a period without commission or a particular arrangement for certain works. Any such variation:</span></p>\n<ul><li>(a) must be agreed in writing (email is sufficient) by both parties before it applies;</li><li>(b) is recorded by PlotArt with the Artist’s account; and</li><li>(c) applies only for the period, sales or works it states. Everything else in this agreement continues to apply.</li></ul>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c13.2\"><span class=\"n\">13.2</span><span>A variation does not need to be published, and is not offered to other artists by reason of being agreed with one.</span></p>\n<h2 id=\"14-artwork-accuracy-and-permissions\">14. Artwork, accuracy and permissions</h2>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c14.1\"><span class=\"n\">14.1</span><span>The Artist confirms that they own, or are authorised to offer, each listed work, and have the rights needed to provide its images and accompanying material.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c14.2\"><span class=\"n\">14.2</span><span>The Artist will supply accurate titles, medium, dimensions, year, price, framing and availability information, will promptly correct inaccuracies, and will mark a work as sold or withdrawn in PlotArt Studio, where the change takes effect straight away.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c14.3\"><span class=\"n\">14.3</span><span>PlotArt welcomes original digital work and AI-assisted practice. The Artist will disclose any meaningful use of AI in making a work. Images generated entirely from prompts are not automatically eligible as original artist-created artwork; PlotArt decides their eligibility.</span></p>\n<h2 id=\"15-copyright-and-image-licence\">15. Copyright and image licence</h2>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c15.1\"><span class=\"n\">15.1</span><span>Copyright, moral rights and ownership of the artworks, images and texts remain with the Artist or the respective rights holders. This agreement transfers no intellectual property to PlotArt.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c15.2\"><span class=\"n\">15.2</span><span>PlotArt uses the Artist’s images and information only as the Licence permits: non-exclusively and royalty-free, on PlotArt and PlotNua web pages. Any promotional use beyond those pages needs the Artist’s separate permission for each use.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c15.3\"><span class=\"n\">15.3</span><span>PlotArt will not sell or sublicense the Artist’s images, make products from them, add them to stock libraries, or use them to train artificial-intelligence models.</span></p>\n<h2 id=\"16-plotart-studio-and-publication\">16. PlotArt Studio and publication</h2>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c16.1\"><span class=\"n\">16.1</span><span>The Artist manages the gallery through PlotArt Studio, signed in with a one-time code sent to the Artist’s email address. Changes the Artist submits count as the Artist’s approval.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c16.2\"><span class=\"n\">16.2</span><span>PlotArt will not first publish the gallery until the Artist has submitted its preview in PlotArt Studio. Later changes are published as follows:</span></p>\n<ul><li><strong>straight away:</strong> availability (available, reserved, sold), withdrawing a work, the order of works, and whether the gallery shows that the Artist is open for commissions;</li><li><strong>after a quick check by PlotArt:</strong> prices and corrections to existing details;</li><li><strong>after review by PlotArt:</strong> new works, new or replacement photographs, the biography and the portrait.</li></ul>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c16.3\"><span class=\"n\">16.3</span><span>PlotArt may ask the Artist to correct, or may decline, a change that does not meet this agreement, the Licence or the photography guide, and will say why.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c16.4\"><span class=\"n\">16.4</span><span>Participation in the Mobile Gallery, the Living Gallery, Art for Hire or any physical display needs a separate written arrangement. Care, handling, insurance and transport are discussed for every placement.</span></p>\n<h2 id=\"17-suspension-and-ending\">17. Suspension and ending</h2>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c17.1\"><span class=\"n\">17.1</span><span><strong>By the Artist.</strong> The Artist may end this agreement at any time, in PlotArt Studio or by email. PlotArt removes the public gallery within 14 days.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c17.2\"><span class=\"n\">17.2</span><span><strong>By PlotArt on notice.</strong> PlotArt may end this agreement on at least 60 days’ written notice, giving its reasons.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c17.3\"><span class=\"n\">17.3</span><span><strong>Unpaid commission: suspension.</strong> If an invoice remains unpaid 14 days after its due date, PlotArt will send a reminder. If it remains unpaid 30 days after the reminder, PlotArt may suspend new introductions and the public display of the Artist’s gallery. PlotArt will first give at least 14 days’ written notice stating the amount owed and the reason. The suspension ends as soon as payment is received.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c17.4\"><span class=\"n\">17.4</span><span><strong>Unpaid commission: ending.</strong> If commission remains materially unpaid after a suspension notice under clause 17.3, PlotArt may end this agreement for persistent non-payment. It does so only after giving a final written notice that:</span></p>\n<ul><li>states the amount owed;</li><li>offers the Artist at least 30 days to pay, or to agree a reasonable payment arrangement; and</li><li>states that the agreement will end if neither happens.</li></ul>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c17.5\"><span class=\"n\">17.5</span><span><strong>Breach and unlawful content.</strong> PlotArt may end this agreement for another serious or repeated breach after giving the Artist a reasonable opportunity to put it right. It may promptly suspend or remove unlawful or materially infringing content, giving its reasons, unless the law prevents it.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c17.6\"><span class=\"n\">17.6</span><span><strong>What continues after ending.</strong> These survive the end of this agreement:</span></p>\n<ul><li>commission obligations under clauses 5 and 8 to 12 for Qualifying Sales covered by clause 11.2;</li><li>PlotArt’s record-keeping under clause 18.3; and</li><li>obligations already owed to collectors.</li></ul>\n<p>Neither party owes any fee for ending this agreement.</p>\n<h2 id=\"18-information-records-and-communications\">18. Information, records and communications</h2>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c18.1\"><span class=\"n\">18.1</span><span>PlotArt processes artist, enquiry and sale-report information in accordance with its privacy notice at plotnua.ie/privacy.html.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c18.2\"><span class=\"n\">18.2</span><span>Sale reports contain no collector contact details.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c18.3\"><span class=\"n\">18.3</span><span><strong>Commission records.</strong> PlotArt keeps acceptance records, sale reports, commission invoices and payment records for as long as this agreement lasts and for six years after it ends or, if later, six years after the last commission invoice or payment under it, then deletes them unless the law requires otherwise. These are records PlotArt needs to meet its legal and accounting obligations and to establish or defend legal claims, within clause 6.6 of the Licence. The 12-month deletion of account and gallery records in clause 6.5 of the Licence does not apply to them.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c18.4\"><span class=\"n\">18.4</span><span><strong>Questions and complaints.</strong> Questions or complaints about this agreement, commission or the gallery can be sent to hello@plotnua.ie. PlotArt will respond within 14 days.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c18.5\"><span class=\"n\">18.5</span><span>Notices are given by email, to the address the Artist uses for PlotArt Studio and to hello@plotnua.ie.</span></p>\n<h2 id=\"19-responsibility-and-governing-law\">19. Responsibility and governing law</h2>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c19.1\"><span class=\"n\">19.1</span><span>Each party remains responsible for its own acts and obligations, including its own tax.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c19.2\"><span class=\"n\">19.2</span><span>Nothing in this agreement excludes or limits any liability that cannot lawfully be excluded or limited, or affects statutory rights.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c19.3\"><span class=\"n\">19.3</span><span>This agreement is governed by the law of Ireland, and the courts of Ireland have jurisdiction. This does not take away any protection the Artist has under mandatory law where the Artist lives.</span></p>\n<h2 id=\"20-changes-to-this-agreement\">20. Changes to this agreement</h2>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c20.1\"><span class=\"n\">20.1</span><span>PlotArt may propose changes as a new, identified version in PlotArt Studio, giving at least 30 days’ notice. A new version applies to the Artist only when the Artist expressly accepts it there.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c20.2\"><span class=\"n\">20.2</span><span>No change may raise the commission rate, lengthen the Attribution Period, introduce a fee, or alter commission on introductions already made, without the Artist’s express acceptance.</span></p>\n<h2 id=\"21-general\">21. General</h2>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c21.1\"><span class=\"n\">21.1</span><span>This agreement, the Licence and any written variation under clause 13 form the whole agreement between PlotArt and the Artist about the Artist’s gallery.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c21.2\"><span class=\"n\">21.2</span><span>This agreement does not create a partnership, employment or agency. Neither party can bind the other.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c21.3\"><span class=\"n\">21.3</span><span>PlotArt may transfer this agreement only to a business that takes over PlotArt, on the same terms, and will tell the Artist by email.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c21.4\"><span class=\"n\">21.4</span><span>If any part of this agreement is found unenforceable, the rest continues to apply.</span></p>\n<h2 id=\"acceptance-in-plotart-studio\">Acceptance in PlotArt Studio</h2>\n<p>The Artist accepts this agreement in PlotArt Studio by ticking this statement:</p>\n<blockquote>“I have read and accept the PlotArt Gallery Artist Agreement PA-GAA-2026-11, including the Gallery Publication and Image Licence PA-GPIL-2026-11.”</blockquote>\n</article>\n<footer>PlotArt Gallery Artist Agreement  ·  PA-GAA-2026-11 · plotnua.ie · hello@plotnua.ie</footer></main></body></html>\n","pdf_b64":"","html_sha256":"60bab19a949add256b53162b2819c610985e02c878eadd45f274a1e1fb39d038","pdf_sha256":"a7f943f391674f8df1f430be4ae575c531c6752c75c44f186950934389f51781"}};
export const HIRE_TERMS = {};
export const CHECKOUT_HTML = "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en-IE\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover\">\n<title>PlotArt Studio · Payment pilot</title>\n<meta name=\"robots\" content=\"noindex, nofollow\">\n<meta name=\"theme-color\" content=\"#1B1C1E\">\n<link rel=\"icon\" href=\"/assets/brand/plotart-favicon-32.png\" type=\"image/png\" sizes=\"32x32\">\n<link rel=\"apple-touch-icon\" href=\"/assets/brand/plotart-apple-touch-180.png\">\n<link rel=\"preconnect\" href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com\">\n<link rel=\"preconnect\" href=\"https://fonts.gstatic.com\" crossorigin>\n<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Instrument+Serif:ital@0;1&family=Hanken+Grotesk:wght@400;500;600;700&display=swap\">\n<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/assets/plotart.css\">\n<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/assets/studio.css\">\n</head>\n<body class=\"pa st\">\n<header class=\"st-top\"><div class=\"st-top-in\"><a class=\"st-word\" href=\"/\" aria-label=\"PlotArt Payment pilot\"><img class=\"st-logo\" src=\"/assets/brand/plotart-logo-stacked.svg\" width=\"53\" height=\"52\" alt=\"\"><small>Payment pilot</small></a><div class=\"st-who\" id=\"who\"></div></div>\n<nav class=\"st-tabs\" aria-label=\"Studio\"><a href=\"/\">Studio</a></nav></header>\n<main class=\"st-main\" id=\"app\" aria-live=\"polite\"><p class=\"st-muted\">Loading…</p></main>\n<div class=\"st-saved\" id=\"saved\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"></div>\n<script src=\"/assets/checkout-pilot.js\" defer></script>\n</body>\n</html>\n";
export const CHECKOUT_JS = "/* PlotArt Studio · payment pilot page (development 16 Nov 2026; TEST MODE). One small page for both roles:\n   /admin/checkout (founder) and /checkout-pilot (artist). Not linked from the Studio tabs: reached by its address only. */\n(() => {\n  const founder = location.pathname.startsWith('/admin');\n  const base = founder ? '/api/admin/checkout' : '/api/checkout';\n  const app = document.getElementById('app');\n  const esc = s => String(s ?? '').replace(/[&<>\"']/g, c => ({ '&': '&amp;', '<': '&lt;', '>': '&gt;', '\"': '&quot;', \"'\": '&#39;' })[c]);\n  const eur = c => c == null ? '—' : '€' + (c / 100).toFixed(2);\n  const api = async (method, path, body) => {\n    const r = await fetch(path, { method, headers: { 'X-Studio': '1', 'Content-Type': 'application/json' }, body: body === undefined ? undefined : JSON.stringify(body) });\n    const j = await r.json().catch(() => ({ ok: false, error: 'Unreadable response' }));\n    if (!j.ok) throw new Error(j.error || 'Refused');\n    return j;\n  };\n  const say = m => { const s = document.getElementById('saved'); s.textContent = m; s.classList.add('on'); setTimeout(() => s.classList.remove('on'), 4000); };\n  /* Errors are written into the page (role=\"alert\"): next to the form that was submitted, else at the top. Browser dialogs\n     (alert, prompt, confirm) are not used for the founder's quote and refund steps: some browsers, including embedded ones,\n     suppress them, which silently sent empty answers (20 Nov 2026, deployed TEST purchase). */\n  const showError = (ev, msg) => {\n    const f = ev && ev.target && ev.target.closest && ev.target.closest('form'), box = (f && f.querySelector('[data-err]')) || document.getElementById('page-error');\n    if (box) { box.textContent = msg; box.hidden = false; box.focus && box.focus(); }\n  };\n  const act = fn => async ev => { ev.preventDefault(); const f = ev.target.closest && ev.target.closest('form'), box = f && f.querySelector('[data-err]');\n    if (box) { box.textContent = ''; box.hidden = true; }\n    const btn = f && f.querySelector('button[type=submit], button:not([type])'); if (btn) btn.disabled = true;\n    try { await fn(ev); } catch (e) { showError(ev, e.message); } finally { if (btn && btn.isConnected) btn.disabled = false; } };\n  /* \"12.50\" → 1250. Whole euro or euro and cents only; never via floating point. */\n  const toCents = (v, what) => { const t = String(v ?? '').trim().replace(',', '.');\n    if (!/^\\d{1,7}(\\.\\d{1,2})?$/.test(t)) throw new Error(`Enter the ${what} in euro, for example 12.50`);\n    const [w, c = ''] = t.split('.'); return Number(w) * 100 + Number((c + '00').slice(0, 2)); };\n  let ISSUED = null;   // the one-time buyer link, kept on screen until the page is left or reloaded\n  const todayIE = () => new Intl.DateTimeFormat('en-CA', { timeZone: 'Europe/Dublin' }).format(new Date());\n  const plusDaysIE = n => new Intl.DateTimeFormat('en-CA', { timeZone: 'Europe/Dublin' }).format(new Date(Date.now() + n * 86400_000));\n  const isDate = v => /^\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2}$/.test(String(v || ''));\n  /* One collapsible on-page form. Errors appear inside it (role=\"alert\"); an irreversible financial step carries its own\n     confirmation tick, checked again before anything is sent. No browser dialogs anywhere on this page (20 Nov 2026). */\n  const step = (kind, summary, body, submit, { open = false, extra = '' } = {}) =>\n    `<details class=\"st-step\"${open ? ' open' : ''}${extra}><summary>${summary}</summary><form data-f=\"${kind}\" novalidate>${body}\n      <p class=\"st-err\" role=\"alert\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-err hidden></p><button type=\"submit\">${submit}</button></form></details>`;\n  const field = (id, label, input) => `<label for=\"${id}\">${label}</label> ${input}`;\n  const tick = (label) => `<label><input type=\"checkbox\" name=\"confirm\" required> ${label}</label>`;\n  const need = (cond, msg) => { if (!cond) throw new Error(msg); };\n  // One owed item's payments, each bank transfer not yet returned with its \"Transfer returned…\" form (shown once: the\n  // control disappears when a return is recorded, and the server refuses a second return of the same transfer).\n  const payRow = (w, cols) => w.payments.length ? `<tr data-id=\"${esc(w.order_id)}\"><td></td><td colspan=\"${cols}\"><small>${w.payments.map(x => `${eur(x.cents)} · ${esc(x.method.replace(/_/g, ' '))}${x.executed_on ? ` · executed ${esc(x.executed_on)}` : ''} · ref ${esc(x.reference)} · recorded by ${esc(x.recorded_by)} at ${esc(x.at)}${x.returned_on ? ` · <strong>returned ${esc(x.returned_on)}</strong> (${esc(x.returned_reason)})` : x.method === 'bank_transfer' ? step('shortfallreturned', 'Transfer returned…', `<input type=\"hidden\" name=\"payment_id\" value=\"${esc(x.id)}\">\n            ${field(`sr-on-${esc(x.id)}`, 'Date the bank shows it returned', `<input id=\"sr-on-${esc(x.id)}\" name=\"returned_on\" type=\"date\" min=\"${esc(x.executed_on || '')}\" max=\"${todayIE()}\" required>`)}\n            ${field(`sr-why-${esc(x.id)}`, 'Reason the bank gave (5–300 characters, no bank details)', `<input id=\"sr-why-${esc(x.id)}\" name=\"reason\" maxlength=\"300\" required>`)}\n            ${tick(`The bank shows this ${eur(x.cents)} transfer as returned. The amount becomes owed again.`)}`, 'Record returned transfer') : ''}`).join('<br>')}</small></td></tr>` : '';\n  const HOLD_BASES = [['dispute', 'Dispute'], ['claim', 'Claim'], ['revenue_enquiry', 'Revenue enquiry'], ['investigation', 'Investigation'], ['litigation', 'Litigation'], ['data_subject_request', 'Data subject request'], ['other', 'Other']];\n  const TEMPLATE = { collection_county: '', destination: '', unpacked_cm: '', packed_cm: '', weight_kg: 0, medium: '', framing: '', glazing: '', condition: '', access_notes: null,\n    organiser: 'artist', packer: 'artist', transport_booker: 'artist', transport_contracting_party: 'artist', transport_payer: 'artist', transporter_name: '',\n    installation: 'not_applicable', import_costs: 'not_applicable', cover_type: 'transit_insurance', cover_provider: '', covered_value_cents: 0, valuation_basis: '',\n    excess_cents: null, exclusions: null, cover_period: '', claims_contact: '', insured_party: 'transporter', cover_confirmation_ref: '', cover_confirmed_by: '', cover_confirmed_on: new Date().toISOString().slice(0, 10), delivery_window: '', tracking: '', signed_receipt: true, condition_photos: true,\n    return_method: '', return_address: '', return_cost_cents: 0, return_cost_basis: 'estimated_maximum', return_arranged_by: 'buyer', shipment_confirmation_ref: '', shipment_confirmed_by: '', shipment_confirmed_on: new Date().toISOString().slice(0, 10) };\n\n  /* The artist's statement: every amount on its own line, nothing netted silently (fee model B). */\n  function statementTable(st) {\n    const row = (label, c, sign = '', strong = false) => c || strong ? `<tr><td>${strong ? '<strong>' : ''}${label}${strong ? '</strong>' : ''}</td><td style=\"text-align:right\">${sign}${eur(Math.abs(c))}</td></tr>` : '';\n    return `<details open><summary>Statement</summary><table class=\"st-table\" style=\"max-width:34rem\">\n      ${row('Gross payment from the buyer', st.gross_payment, '', true)}\n      ${row('of which artwork', st.of_which_artwork)}${row('of which delivery', st.of_which_delivery)}\n      ${row('PlotArt commission (on the artwork only)', st.plotart_commission, '− ')}\n      ${row('Commission refunded by PlotArt', st.commission_refunded, '+ ')}\n      ${row('Stripe processing fee (whole payment)', st.stripe_processing_fee, '− ')}\n      ${row('VAT charged by Stripe on that fee', st.vat_on_processing_fee, '− ')}\n      ${row('Processing fee and VAT reimbursed by PlotArt', st.processing_reimbursed_by_plotart, '+ ')}\n      ${row('Paid directly by PlotArt (shortfall)', st.shortfall_paid_by_plotart, '+ ')}\n      ${row('Other Stripe fees on this payment (not reimbursed)', st.other_stripe_fees_not_reimbursed, '− ')}\n      ${row('Refunded to the buyer', st.refunded_to_buyer, '− ')}\n      ${row('Disputes (net)', st.disputes_net, st.disputes_net < 0 ? '− ' : '+ ')}\n      ${row('Stripe dispute fees (incl. VAT)', st.dispute_fees_charged_by_stripe, '− ')}${row('Dispute fees returned by Stripe', st.dispute_fees_returned_by_stripe, '+ ')}\n      ${row('Net proceeds', st.net_proceeds, st.net_proceeds < 0 ? '− ' : '', true)}\n      ${st.shortfall_still_owed_by_plotart ? row('Owed by PlotArt, not yet paid (shortfall)', st.shortfall_still_owed_by_plotart, '', true) : ''}\n      ${st.commission_refund_owed ? row('Commission to be returned after a lost dispute, not yet returned', st.commission_refund_owed, '', true) : ''}\n      </table><small class=\"st-muted\">Processing: ${esc(String(st.processing_status).replace(/_/g, ' '))}. Dispute fees: ${esc(st.dispute_fees_status)}. ${esc(st.not_included)}</small></details>`;\n  }\n  /* Issue buyer quote (founder). Same request and server rules as before: 1–7 days; the linked-purchases answer is required\n     and only \"not linked\" lets the server issue the quote. */\n  function issueForm(o) {\n    const k = esc(o.id);\n    return `<details class=\"st-step\" open><summary>Issue buyer quote…</summary><form data-f=\"issue\" novalidate>\n      <p class=\"st-muted\">Artwork ${eur(o.artwork_cents)} · delivery ${eur(o.delivery_cents)} · <strong>buyer pays ${eur(o.total_cents)}</strong> · PlotArt commission ${eur(o.commission_cents)} · quote version ${o.quote_version}, approved by the artist.</p>\n      <label for=\"iq-days-${k}\">Quote valid for (days, 1–7)</label> <input id=\"iq-days-${k}\" name=\"days\" type=\"number\" inputmode=\"numeric\" min=\"1\" max=\"7\" step=\"1\" value=\"3\" required>\n      <fieldset><legend>Linked purchases: as far as you know, is this purchase linked to other purchases by this buyer or anyone acting with them (other email addresses, household, business, agents, staged payments)?</legend>\n        <label><input type=\"radio\" name=\"linked\" value=\"not_linked\" required> Not linked, as far as I know</label>\n        <label><input type=\"radio\" name=\"linked\" value=\"linked_or_unsure\"> Linked, or I am not sure (the quote will not be issued)</label></fieldset>\n      <p class=\"st-err\" role=\"alert\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-err hidden></p>\n      <button type=\"submit\">Issue buyer quote</button></form></details>`;\n  }\n  /* Refund (founder). Same request as before: artwork and delivery amounts in cents, and a reason. The server keeps every\n     rule (paid orders only, never more than is still unrefunded, PlotArt's commission share returned under the agreement). */\n  function refundForm(o) {\n    const k = esc(o.id), st = o.statement || {};\n    return `<details class=\"st-step\"><summary>Refund…</summary><form data-f=\"refund\" novalidate>\n      <p class=\"st-muted\">Paid: artwork ${eur(o.artwork_cents)}, delivery ${eur(o.delivery_cents)}${st.refunded_to_buyer ? ` · already refunded ${eur(st.refunded_to_buyer)}` : ''}. Stripe refunds the buyer from the artist’s Stripe account; Studio then returns PlotArt’s commission share as the agreement provides.</p>\n      <label for=\"rf-art-${k}\">Artwork amount to refund (€)</label> <input id=\"rf-art-${k}\" name=\"artwork\" inputmode=\"decimal\" value=\"0.00\" required>\n      <label for=\"rf-del-${k}\">Delivery amount to refund (€)</label> <input id=\"rf-del-${k}\" name=\"delivery\" inputmode=\"decimal\" value=\"0.00\" required>\n      <label for=\"rf-why-${k}\">Reason (shown in the order record)</label> <input id=\"rf-why-${k}\" name=\"reason\" maxlength=\"300\" required>\n      <p data-sum aria-live=\"polite\"></p>\n      <label><input type=\"checkbox\" name=\"confirm\" required> I confirm this refund through Stripe. A refund cannot be undone.</label>\n      <p class=\"st-err\" role=\"alert\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-err hidden></p>\n      <button type=\"submit\">Refund through Stripe</button></form></details>`;\n  }\n  function holdForm(o) { const k = esc(o.id);\n    return step('hold', 'Legal hold…', `<p class=\"st-muted\">Keeps this order’s records beyond the normal retention date while the hold is active. Review it at least every 12 months.</p>\n      ${field(`hd-basis-${k}`, 'Basis', `<select id=\"hd-basis-${k}\" name=\"basis\" required><option value=\"\">Choose…</option>${HOLD_BASES.map(([v, t]) => `<option value=\"${v}\">${t}</option>`).join('')}</select>`)}\n      ${field(`hd-why-${k}`, 'Specific reason (10–1,000 characters)', `<textarea id=\"hd-why-${k}\" name=\"reason\" rows=\"3\" maxlength=\"1000\" required></textarea>`)}\n      ${field(`hd-rv-${k}`, 'Review by (within 12 months)', `<input id=\"hd-rv-${k}\" name=\"review_by\" type=\"date\" min=\"${plusDaysIE(1)}\" max=\"${plusDaysIE(365)}\" required>`)}`, 'Place legal hold'); }\n  function repaidForm(o) { const k = esc(o.id);\n    return step('repaid', 'Record repayment outside Stripe…', `<p class=\"st-muted\">Only when the artist has repaid the buyer directly (not through Stripe). Studio books it as a refund and returns PlotArt’s commission share as the agreement provides.</p>\n      ${field(`rp-art-${k}`, 'Artwork amount repaid (€)', `<input id=\"rp-art-${k}\" name=\"artwork\" inputmode=\"decimal\" value=\"0.00\" required>`)}\n      ${field(`rp-del-${k}`, 'Delivery amount repaid (€)', `<input id=\"rp-del-${k}\" name=\"delivery\" inputmode=\"decimal\" value=\"0.00\" required>`)}\n      ${field(`rp-ev-${k}`, 'Evidence: transfer reference, date and the buyer’s confirmation (no bank details)', `<textarea id=\"rp-ev-${k}\" name=\"evidence\" rows=\"2\" maxlength=\"500\" required></textarea>`)}\n      ${tick('I confirm the buyer has been repaid as described. This is recorded as a refund and cannot be undone.')}`, 'Record repayment'); }\n  function shortfallForm(o) { const k = esc(o.id), out = o.statement.shortfall_still_owed_by_plotart;\n    return step('shortfallpaid', 'Record shortfall paid…', `<p class=\"st-muted\">PlotArt still owes the artist <strong>${eur(out)}</strong> outside Stripe on this order. Record a payment only once PlotArt’s bank shows the transfer as <strong>executed</strong>. Never enter bank details here.</p>\n      ${field(`sp-amt-${k}`, `Amount the bank shows as executed (€, up to ${eur(out)})`, `<input id=\"sp-amt-${k}\" name=\"amount\" inputmode=\"decimal\" required>`)}\n      ${field(`sp-on-${k}`, 'Date the bank shows it executed', `<input id=\"sp-on-${k}\" name=\"executed_on\" type=\"date\" max=\"${todayIE()}\" required>`)}\n      ${field(`sp-ref-${k}`, 'The bank’s transfer reference only (6–200 characters)', `<input id=\"sp-ref-${k}\" name=\"reference\" maxlength=\"200\" required autocomplete=\"off\">`)}\n      ${tick('PlotArt’s bank shows this transfer as executed. Recording it settles the amount owed and tells the artist.')}`, 'Record shortfall paid', { extra: ` data-step=\"shortfallpaid\"` }); }\n  function returnCommissionForm(o) { const k = esc(o.id), due = o.statement.commission_refund_owed;\n    return step('returncommission', 'Return commission (lost dispute)…', `<p class=\"st-muted\">The dispute was lost, so PlotArt returns its commission under PA-GAA 9.1: <strong>${eur(due)}</strong>, through Stripe where the application fee allows, otherwise owed by bank transfer.</p>\n      ${field(`rc-why-${k}`, 'Reason (recorded on the order)', `<input id=\"rc-why-${k}\" name=\"reason\" maxlength=\"300\" value=\"Dispute lost: commission returned under PA-GAA 9.1\" required>`)}\n      ${tick(`Return ${eur(due)} of PlotArt’s commission to the artist. This cannot be undone.`)}`, 'Return commission', { extra: ` data-step=\"returncommission\"` }); }\n  function cancelForm(o) { const k = esc(o.id);\n    return step('cancel', 'Cancel order…', `<p class=\"st-muted\">Cancels this unpaid order and any open quote; the buyer’s link then says it cannot be paid. A paid order is never cancelled: refund it instead.</p>\n      ${field(`cn-why-${k}`, 'Reason (optional, recorded on the order)', `<input id=\"cn-why-${k}\" name=\"reason\" maxlength=\"300\">`)}\n      ${tick('Cancel this order.')}`, 'Cancel order'); }\n  function orderCard(o) {\n    const d = o.delivery;\n    let h = `<section class=\"st-card\" id=\"order-${esc(o.id)}\" data-id=\"${esc(o.id)}\"><h3>${esc(o.reference)} · ${esc(o.artwork && o.artwork.title)} <small class=\"st-muted\">${esc(o.status.replace(/_/g, ' '))}</small></h3>\n      <p>Artwork ${eur(o.artwork_cents)} · delivery ${eur(o.delivery_cents)} · total ${eur(o.total_cents)} · PlotArt commission ${o.commission_bp == null ? '—' : (o.commission_bp / 100).toFixed(2) + '% = ' + eur(o.commission_cents)}\n      ${o.commission_basis ? `<br><small class=\"st-muted\">Basis: ${esc(o.commission_basis.replace(/_/g, ' '))}. ${esc(o.processing_fees)}</small>` : ''}</p>\n      ${o.needs_resolution ? `<p class=\"st-warn\"><strong>Needs resolution:</strong> ${esc(o.needs_resolution)}</p>` : ''}\n      ${o.statement ? statementTable(o.statement) : ''}\n      <p class=\"st-muted\">Quote version ${o.quote_version}${o.artist_approved_version === o.quote_version ? ' · approved by the artist' : ''}${o.quote_expires_at ? ' · expires ' + esc(o.quote_expires_at) : ''} · payment ${esc(o.payment_status)} · fulfilment ${esc(o.fulfilment_status)} · dispute ${esc(o.dispute_status)}</p>`;\n    if (d) h += `<details><summary>Delivery and cover</summary><pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">${esc(JSON.stringify(d, null, 2))}</pre></details>`;\n    if (founder) {\n      if (['draft', 'awaiting_artist', 'quoted', 'checkout_open', 'payment_failed', 'expired'].includes(o.status)) h += `<details><summary>Edit price, delivery and cover (creates a new quote version)</summary><form data-f=\"edit\">\n        <label>Artwork price (cents) <input name=\"artwork_cents\" type=\"number\" min=\"100\" value=\"${o.artwork_cents ?? ''}\"></label>\n        <label>Delivery charge (cents) <input name=\"delivery_cents\" type=\"number\" min=\"0\" value=\"${o.delivery_cents ?? ''}\"></label>\n        <label>Delivery and cover (JSON) <textarea name=\"delivery\" rows=\"14\" style=\"width:100%;font-family:monospace\">${esc(JSON.stringify(d || TEMPLATE, null, 2))}</textarea></label>\n        <label>Commission exclusion <select name=\"exclusion\"><option value=\"\">none</option>${['prior_relationship', 'representing_gallery', 'independent_sale', 'founder_waiver'].map(x => `<option ${o.exclusion === x ? 'selected' : ''}>${x}</option>`).join('')}</select></label>\n        <button>Save as new version</button></form></details>`;\n      const b = [];\n      if (o.status === 'draft') b.push(['send', 'Send to artist for approval']);\n      if (o.status === 'awaiting_artist' && o.artist_approved_version === o.quote_version) h += issueForm(o);\n      const more = [];\n      if (['draft', 'awaiting_artist', 'quoted', 'checkout_open', 'payment_failed', 'expired'].includes(o.status)) more.push(cancelForm(o));\n      if (o.payment_intent || o.status === 'checkout_open') b.push(['reconcile', 'Reconcile with Stripe']);\n      if (o.payment_intent && ['paid', 'dispatched', 'delivered', 'refund_pending', 'disputed', 'refunded'].includes(o.status)) h += refundForm(o);\n      if (['delivered', 'refunded'].includes(o.status)) b.push(['close', 'Close']);\n      if (o.payment_intent) more.push(holdForm(o), repaidForm(o));\n      if (o.payment_intent && o.commission_cents > 0) b.push(['processing', 'Reconcile processing fee']);\n      if (o.statement && o.statement.shortfall_still_owed_by_plotart) more.push(shortfallForm(o));\n      if (o.statement && o.statement.commission_refund_owed) more.push(returnCommissionForm(o));\n      if (o.payment_intent) b.push(['confirmation', 'Re-deliver buyer confirmation']);\n      if (ISSUED && ISSUED.id === o.id) h += `<div class=\"st-card st-issued\" role=\"status\" data-issued><h4>Buyer quote issued (version ${ISSUED.version})</h4>\n        <p><strong>Buyer link, shown once.</strong> Copy it now and send it to the buyer yourself. Studio keeps only a fingerprint of it and cannot show it again.</p>\n        <label>Buyer link <input data-link readonly value=\"${esc(ISSUED.link)}\" style=\"width:100%\" aria-describedby=\"link-note-${esc(o.id)}\"></label>\n        <p><button type=\"button\" data-copy>Copy link</button> <span id=\"link-note-${esc(o.id)}\" class=\"st-muted\" data-copied aria-live=\"polite\"></span></p></div>`;\n      h += `<p>${b.map(([k, t]) => `<button data-a=\"${k}\">${t}</button>`).join(' ')}</p>` + more.join('');\n    } else if (o.status === 'awaiting_artist' && o.artist_approved_version !== o.quote_version) {\n      h += `<form data-f=\"approve\"><p>Please check this quote carefully. Approving confirms each of the following for <em>this shipment</em>:</p>\n        ${[['available', 'The work is available and not sold or promised elsewhere'], ['location', 'The collection location is correct'], ['condition', 'The condition description is accurate'],\n          ['framing', 'Framing and glazing are as described'], ['dimensions', 'Unpacked and packed dimensions and weight are correct'], ['packing_and_handover', 'I agree the packing, transport and cover responsibilities shown'],\n          ['returns', 'The return method, address, cost estimate and who arranges the return are correct'], ['seller_information', 'My seller information (shown to the buyer) is correct and up to date']]\n          .map(([k, t]) => `<label><input type=\"checkbox\" name=\"${k}\"> ${t}</label>`).join('')}\n        <label>Note (optional) <input name=\"note\" maxlength=\"500\"></label><button>Approve this quote (version ${o.quote_version})</button></form>`\n        + step('decline', 'Ask for changes instead…', `<p class=\"st-muted\">The quote goes back to PlotArt as a draft; nothing is sent to the buyer.</p>\n          ${field(`dc-note-${esc(o.id)}`, 'What should change? (optional, up to 500 characters)', `<textarea id=\"dc-note-${esc(o.id)}\" name=\"note\" rows=\"3\" maxlength=\"500\"></textarea>`)}`, 'Ask for changes');\n    }\n    if (['paid', 'dispatched', 'delivered', 'disputed'].includes(o.status)) h += `<form data-f=\"fulfil\"><label>Record <select name=\"kind\"><option>insurance</option><option>dispatched</option><option>tracking</option><option>condition_photos</option><option>delivered</option><option>signed_receipt</option><option>note</option></select></label>\n      <label>Evidence <input name=\"evidence\" maxlength=\"2000\" required placeholder=\"tracking number, receipt or photo reference\"></label><button>Record</button></form>`;\n    return h + '</section>';\n  }\n\n  /* ---------------------------------------------------------------- multi-artist basket (optional; PA-BAA) */\n  let J_BASKET = null;\n  const CENTS = ['covered_value_cents', 'excess_cents', 'return_cost_cents'];\n  const label = k => k.replace(/_cents$/, ' (€)').replace(/_kg$/, ' (kg)').replace(/_cm$/, ' (cm)').replace(/_/g, ' ').replace(/^./, c => c.toUpperCase());\n  const offerForm = (w, bj) => { const d = (w.offer && w.offer.delivery) || {}, F = bj.delivery_fields;\n    const input = (k, t) => { const id = `of-${esc(w.id)}-${k}`, v = d[k], opt = typeof t === 'string' && t.endsWith('?'), ty = typeof t === 'string' ? t.replace('?', '') : t;\n      if (Array.isArray(ty)) return field(id, label(k), `<select id=\"${id}\" name=\"${k}\">${ty.map(x => `<option ${v === x ? 'selected' : ''}>${esc(x)}</option>`).join('')}</select>`);\n      if (ty === 'p') return field(id, label(k), `<select id=\"${id}\" name=\"${k}\">${bj.parties.map(x => `<option value=\"${esc(x)}\" ${v === x ? 'selected' : ''}>${esc(x.replace(/_/g, ' '))}</option>`).join('')}</select>`);\n      if (ty === 'b') return field(id, label(k), `<select id=\"${id}\" name=\"${k}\"><option value=\"true\" ${v === true ? 'selected' : ''}>yes</option><option value=\"false\" ${v === false ? 'selected' : ''}>no</option></select>`);\n      if (ty === 'd') return field(id, label(k), `<input id=\"${id}\" name=\"${k}\" type=\"date\" value=\"${esc(v || '')}\">`);\n      const val = CENTS.includes(k) && typeof v === 'number' ? (v / 100).toFixed(2) : (v ?? '');\n      return field(id, label(k) + (opt ? ' (optional)' : ''), `<input id=\"${id}\" name=\"${k}\" value=\"${esc(val)}\" ${ty === 'n' && !CENTS.includes(k) ? 'inputmode=\"decimal\"' : ''}>`); };\n    return step('offer', w.offer ? 'Change delivery offer…' : 'Set a delivery offer…', `<div data-id=\"${esc(w.id)}\">\n      ${field(`of-${esc(w.id)}-charge`, 'Delivery charge to the buyer (€), anywhere in the Republic of Ireland', `<input id=\"of-${esc(w.id)}-charge\" name=\"charge\" value=\"${w.offer ? (w.offer.delivery_cents / 100).toFixed(2) : ''}\" required>`)}\n      ${Object.entries(F).filter(([k]) => k !== 'destination').map(([k, t]) => input(k, t)).join('')}\n      ${tick('I will sell and deliver this artwork as described, anywhere in the Republic of Ireland, for this delivery charge, with this transit insurance and these return arrangements.')}</div>`, 'Save delivery offer'); };\n  function basketArtist(bj, j) {\n    const m = bj.membership, pc = m.processing_consent || {}, sd = m.seller_disclosure || {};\n    let h = `<section class=\"st-card\" id=\"basket\"><h2>Online purchase through the basket <small class=\"st-muted\">(optional)</small></h2>\n      <p class=\"st-muted\">Buyers can buy your available artworks online, alone or with other artists’ works. You remain the seller and each payment goes to your own Stripe account. Not taking part changes nothing for your gallery listing, enquiries or direct sales.</p>`;\n    if (!bj.addendum) return h + '<p>The basket addendum has not been issued yet.</p></section>';\n    if (!m.current) return h + `<p>Read the <a href=\"/basket-terms/${esc(bj.addendum.doc_id)}.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">${esc(bj.addendum.title)}</a>.</p>\n      <form data-f=\"basket-optin\"><label><input type=\"checkbox\" name=\"accept\" required> ${esc(bj.addendum.statement)}</label><button>Accept and take part</button></form></section>`;\n    h += `<p>You accepted ${esc(m.doc_id)} on ${esc(m.at)}.</p>`;\n    // 1 · seller information shown before payment\n    const si = bj.seller_info;\n    h += `<h3>Seller information shown to buyers before payment</h3>`;\n    if (!si) h += '<p class=\"st-warn\">Complete your seller information above first.</p>';\n    else {\n      h += `<dl class=\"st-dl\">${[['Seller', si.shown.legal_name + (si.shown.trading_name ? ` (trading as ${si.shown.trading_name})` : '')], ['Address', si.shown.address], ['Returns and complaints', si.shown.returns_address], ['Email', si.shown.email], ['Telephone', si.shown.phone], ['VAT number', si.shown.vat_number]].filter(([, v]) => v).map(([t, v]) => `<dt>${esc(t)}</dt><dd>${esc(v)}</dd>`).join('')}</dl>`;\n      h += sd.valid ? `<p>Confirmed on ${esc(sd.at)}. <button data-a2=\"withdraw-disclosure\">Withdraw (stops online purchase)</button></p>`\n        : `${sd.changed_since ? '<p class=\"st-warn\">Your seller information has changed since you confirmed it: confirm again to keep your works online.</p>' : ''}<form data-f=\"basket-disclosure\"><label><input type=\"checkbox\" name=\"accept\" required> ${esc(bj.disclosure_statement)}</label><button>Confirm</button></form>`;\n    }\n    // 2 · commission-free works: the separate processing-fee consent\n    if (bj.founding) {\n      h += `<h3>Your commission-free artworks <small class=\"st-muted\">(optional, separate consent)</small></h3>`;\n      h += pc.valid ? `<p>You agreed on ${esc(pc.at)} that your commission-free artworks may be bought online, with Stripe’s processing fees deducted from your Stripe balance and 0% PlotArt commission. <button data-a2=\"withdraw-basket-processing\">Withdraw this consent</button></p>`\n        : `<p class=\"st-muted\">Without this consent your commission-free artworks stay on enquiry and direct sale, as now.</p><form data-f=\"basket-processing\"><p style=\"white-space:pre-line\">${esc(bj.processing_statement)}</p><label><input type=\"checkbox\" name=\"accept\" required> I agree to the statement above.</label><button>Give this consent</button></form>`;\n    }\n    // 3 · delivery offers, per artwork\n    h += `<h3>Delivery offers</h3><p class=\"st-muted\">An artwork can be bought online only with a delivery offer you have approved, including transit insurance for at least its price.</p><ul>`;\n    for (const w of bj.works) h += `<li data-id=\"${esc(w.id)}\"><strong>${esc(w.title)}</strong> ${w.price_eur ? '€' + esc(w.price_eur) : '<small class=\"st-muted\">price on request</small>'} · ${esc(w.availability)}\n      · ${w.offer ? `delivery ${eur(w.offer.delivery_cents)} (version ${esc(w.offer.version)}) <button data-withdraw-offer=\"${esc(w.id)}\">Withdraw</button>` : '<small class=\"st-muted\">no delivery offer</small>'}${offerForm(w, bj)}</li>`;\n    h += `</ul>` + step('basket-leave', 'Stop online purchase…', `<p class=\"st-muted\">Your artworks are no longer offered in the basket. Baskets already paid or being paid are completed.</p>${tick('Stop online purchase of my artworks.')}`, 'Stop');\n    return h + '</section>';\n  }\n  function basketFounder(bj) {\n    return `<section class=\"st-card\" id=\"basket-readiness\"><h2>Basket readiness <small class=\"st-muted\">commission-free works: ${esc(bj.commission_free_policy.replace(/_/g, ' '))}${bj.consents_installed ? '' : ' · migration 0020 not installed'}</small></h2>\n      <table class=\"st-table\"><tr><th>Artist</th><th>Stripe</th><th>Addendum</th><th>Seller info shown</th><th>Processing-fee consent</th><th>Offers</th><th>Missing</th></tr>\n      ${bj.artists.map(a => `<tr><td>${esc(a.display_name)}${a.founding ? ' <small>(Founding)</small>' : ''}</td><td>${esc(a.stripe)}</td><td>${esc(a.basket_addendum || '—')}${a.basket_addendum && !a.basket_current ? ' (old)' : ''}</td>\n        <td>${a.seller_disclosure.valid ? 'confirmed ' + esc(a.seller_disclosure.at) : a.seller_disclosure.changed_since ? 'changed since confirmed' : '—'}</td>\n        <td>${a.founding ? (a.processing_consent.valid ? 'given ' + esc(a.processing_consent.at) + ' (' + esc(a.processing_consent.doc_id) + ')' : a.processing_consent.given ? 'given for an older addendum' : 'none') : 'not needed'}</td>\n        <td>${esc(a.delivery_offers)}</td><td>${a.missing.length ? esc(a.missing.join(', ')) : 'ready'}</td></tr>`).join('')}</table></section>`;\n  }\n\n  async function load() {\n    const j = await api('GET', base);\n    if (!j.installed) { app.innerHTML = '<h1>Payment pilot</h1><p>The payment pilot is not installed.</p>'; return; }\n    let h = `<h1>Payment pilot <small class=\"st-muted\">(${j.switches && j.switches.live ? 'LIVE: real payments' : 'Stripe test mode'})</small></h1><p id=\"page-error\" class=\"st-err\" role=\"alert\" tabindex=\"-1\" hidden></p>`;\n    const sw = j.switches;\n    h += `<p class=\"st-muted\">Pilot ${sw.enabled ? (sw.live ? 'switched ON (LIVE: real card payments)' : 'switched ON (test mode)') : 'switched OFF'}${founder && sw.key_problem ? ' · ' + esc(sw.key_problem) : ''}.${sw.live ? '' : ' No live payment can be taken.'}</p>`;\n    if (founder) {\n      const pz = j.pause || { paused: false }, ab = j.absence || { items: [], open_sessions: [], quotes_awaiting_payment: [] };\n      h += `<section id=\"pause-control\" class=\"st-card ${pz.paused ? 'st-paused' : ''}\"><h2>${esc(pz.label || 'Pause new quotes and payments')} <span class=\"st-badge\">${pz.paused ? 'PAUSED' : 'Not paused'}</span></h2>\n        ${pz.paused ? `<p><strong>Paused since ${esc(new Date(pz.since).toLocaleString('en-IE', { timeZone: 'Europe/Dublin', dateStyle: 'medium', timeStyle: 'short' }))}</strong> · expected back ${esc(pz.return_on)}${pz.note ? ` · ${esc(pz.note)}` : ''}</p><p><button data-pause=\"0\">Resume new quotes and payments</button></p>`\n          : `<form data-f=\"pause\"><label>Back on (Irish date) <input type=\"date\" name=\"return_on\" required></label> <label>Note (optional) <input name=\"note\" maxlength=\"300\"></label> <button>Pause new quotes and payments</button></form>`}\n        <p class=\"st-muted\">${esc(pz.explanation || '')}</p>\n        <details ${pz.paused ? 'open' : ''}><summary>Absence checklist — ${ab.quotes_awaiting_payment.length} quote(s) awaiting payment (${ab.open_sessions.length} with a Stripe page open), ${ab.items.length} item(s) due before ${esc(ab.horizon || '')}${ab.assumed_return ? ' (preview, assumed return date)' : ''}</summary>\n          <p class=\"st-muted\">${esc(ab.horizon_note || '')}</p>\n          ${ab.quotes_awaiting_payment.length ? `<h3>Quotes awaiting payment</h3><table class=\"st-table\"><tr><th>Quote</th><th>Payment status</th><th>Quote expiry</th></tr>${ab.quotes_awaiting_payment.map(x => `<tr><td><a href=\"#order-${esc(x.id)}\">${esc(x.reference)}</a></td><td><strong>${x.payment === 'stripe_page_open' ? 'Stripe payment page open' : 'Payment not started'}</strong><br>${esc(x.payment_status)}</td><td>${esc(x.quote_expiry)}</td></tr>`).join('')}</table>` : '<p class=\"st-muted\">No quotes awaiting payment.</p>'}\n          ${ab.items.length ? `<h3>Due before you are back — needs action before you leave</h3><table class=\"st-table\"><tr><th>Order</th><th>What</th><th>Amount</th><th>Due</th><th>Action</th></tr>${ab.items.map(x => `<tr><td><a href=\"#order-${esc(x.order_id)}\">${esc(x.reference)}</a></td><td>${esc(x.what)}${x.note ? `<br><small class=\"st-muted\">${esc(x.note)}</small>` : ''}</td><td>${esc(x.amount)}</td><td>${esc(x.due_label)}</td><td><strong>${esc(x.action)}</strong></td></tr>`).join('')}</table>` : '<p class=\"st-muted\">Nothing falls due before you are back.</p>'}\n        </details></section>`;\n      const fa = j.founder_alerts || { items: [], unread: 0, open: 0, follow_ups_due: 0, note: '' };\n      h += `<section id=\"founder-alerts\" class=\"st-card\"><h2>Founder alerts <span class=\"st-badge\">${fa.unread} unread</span> <small class=\"st-muted\">${fa.open} open · ${fa.follow_ups_due} follow-up${fa.follow_ups_due === 1 ? '' : 's'} due</small></h2>\n        <p class=\"st-muted\">${esc(fa.note)}</p>`;\n      const short = t => t.length > 180 ? t.slice(0, 177) + '…' : t;\n      const rowA = x => `<tr data-alert=\"${x.id}\" class=\"${x.read ? '' : 'st-unread'} ${x.follow_up_due || (x.state === 'open' && /OVERDUE/.test(x.due_label)) ? 'st-warn' : ''}\">\n          <td>${x.read ? 'Read' : '<strong>Unread</strong>'}<br><small>${x.state === 'open' ? 'Open' : 'Resolved'}</small></td><td><small>${esc(x.recorded_irish)}<br>${esc(x.delivery)}</small></td>\n          <td>${esc(x.reason)}<br><small class=\"st-muted\" title=\"${esc(x.detail)}\">${esc(short(x.detail))}</small></td><td>${x.link ? `<a href=\"${esc(x.link)}\">${esc(x.reference || x.order_id)}</a>` : '—'}</td>\n          <td>${esc(x.amount_label)}</td><td>${esc(x.due_label)}</td>\n          <td><input data-next=\"${x.id}\" maxlength=\"300\" placeholder=\"Next action\" value=\"${esc(x.next_action || '')}\"> <input data-fu=\"${x.id}\" type=\"date\" value=\"${esc(x.follow_up_on || '')}\">${x.follow_up_due ? '<br><strong>Follow-up due</strong>' : ''}</td>\n          <td><button data-alert-save=\"${x.id}\">Save</button> <button data-alert-read=\"${x.id}\" data-v=\"${x.read ? '0' : '1'}\">${x.read ? 'Mark unread' : 'Mark read'}</button></td></tr>`;\n      const head = '<tr><th></th><th>Recorded</th><th>Reason</th><th>Order</th><th>Outstanding now</th><th>Due (Irish date)</th><th>Next action</th><th></th></tr>';\n      const openA = fa.items.filter(x => x.state === 'open').sort((p, q) => (q.follow_up_due - p.follow_up_due) || (p.read - q.read)), doneA = fa.items.filter(x => x.state !== 'open');\n      h += openA.length ? `<table class=\"st-table\">${head}${openA.map(rowA).join('')}</table>` : '<p class=\"st-muted\">Nothing open.</p>';\n      if (doneA.length) h += `<details><summary>Resolved items (${doneA.length}${doneA.some(x => !x.read) ? `, ${doneA.filter(x => !x.read).length} unread` : ''})</summary><table class=\"st-table\">${head}${doneA.map(rowA).join('')}</table></details>`;\n      h += `</section>`;\n      h += `<p>Addendum: ${esc(j.addendum || 'not issued')} · Buyer terms: ${esc(j.buyer_terms || 'not issued')}</p><h2>Artists who opted in</h2>`;\n      h += j.artists.length ? `<ul>${j.artists.map(a => `<li>${esc(a.display_name)} — ${a.membership.opted_in ? 'opted in' : 'left'} · Stripe ${a.membership.account ? (a.membership.ready ? 'ready' : 'onboarding incomplete') : 'not connected'}\n        ${a.membership.account ? `<button data-refresh=\"${esc(a.id)}\">Refresh</button>` : ''}</li>`).join('')}</ul>` : '<p class=\"st-muted\">Nobody yet. Artists opt in themselves at /checkout-pilot.</p>';\n      h += `<h2>New order from an enquiry</h2><form data-f=\"create\"><label>Artist <select name=\"artist_id\">${j.artists.filter(a => a.membership.opted_in).map(a => `<option value=\"${esc(a.id)}\">${esc(a.display_name)}</option>`).join('')}</select></label>\n        <label>Artwork id <input name=\"artwork_id\" required></label><label>Enquiry reference <input name=\"enquiry_ref\" required placeholder=\"PA-E-…\"></label>\n        <label>Buyer email <input name=\"buyer_email\" type=\"email\" required></label><button>Create draft</button></form>`;\n      if (j.pending_refunds.length) h += `<h2>Refunds waiting for an artist’s Stripe balance</h2><ul>${j.pending_refunds.map(r => `<li class=\"${r.urgency === 'new' ? '' : 'st-warn'}\">${esc(r.reference)} · ${eur(r.amount_cents)} · pending ${r.days_pending} days · Stripe cancels it on ${esc(r.stripe_fails_it_by)} (${esc(r.urgency)})</li>`).join('')}</ul>\n        <details><summary>What the artist does</summary><ol>${j.refund_funding_steps.map(x => `<li>${esc(x)}</li>`).join('')}</ol></details>`;\n      h += `<h2>Amounts owed to artists</h2><p class=\"st-muted\">${esc(j.deadlines.note)}</p>${j.owed.length ? `<table class=\"st-table\"><tr><th>Order</th><th>Artist</th><th>What</th><th>Owed</th><th>Paid</th><th>Outstanding</th><th>Age</th><th>Due</th><th>Reminders</th><th></th></tr>\n        ${j.owed.map(w => `<tr data-id=\"${esc(w.order_id)}\" class=\"${w.status === 'overdue' ? 'st-warn' : ''}\"><td>${esc(w.reference)}</td><td>${esc(w.artist_name)}</td><td>${esc(w.kind.replace(/_/g, ' '))}<br><small class=\"st-muted\">${esc(w.reason)}</small></td>\n          <td>${eur(w.cents)}</td><td>${eur(w.settled_cents)}</td><td><strong>${eur(w.outstanding_cents)}</strong></td><td>${w.age_days} d</td><td>${esc(w.due_label || w.due_date)}${w.due_provisional ? ' <em>(provisional)</em>' : ''}<br><small class=\"st-muted\">${esc(w.due_rule)}</small>${w.due_review ? `<br><strong>For review:</strong> <small>${esc(w.due_review)}</small>` : ''}</td>\n          <td>${esc(w.reminders.join(', ') || '—')}</td><td><a href=\"#order-${esc(w.order_id)}\" data-open=\"${w.kind === 'lost_dispute_commission' ? 'returncommission' : 'shortfallpaid'}\">${w.kind === 'lost_dispute_commission' ? 'Return commission…' : 'Record payment…'}</a></td></tr>\n          ${payRow(w, 9)}`).join('')}</table>` : '<p class=\"st-muted\">Nothing owed.</p>'}\n        ${(j.owed_returnable || []).length ? `<h3>Settled by bank transfer: record a returned transfer</h3><p class=\"st-muted\">Fully paid amounts leave the list above. If the bank later returns one of these transfers (executed in the last ${esc(String(j.return_window_days || 90))} days), record it here; the amount becomes owed again.</p>\n          <table class=\"st-table\" data-owed-returnable><tr><th>Order</th><th>Artist</th><th>What</th><th>Owed</th><th>Paid</th></tr>\n          ${j.owed_returnable.map(w => `<tr data-id=\"${esc(w.order_id)}\"><td>${esc(w.reference)}</td><td>${esc(w.artist_name)}</td><td>${esc(w.kind.replace(/_/g, ' '))}</td><td>${eur(w.cents)}</td><td>${eur(w.settled_cents)}</td></tr>${payRow(w, 4)}`).join('')}</table>` : ''}\n        ${(j.reimbursements || []).length ? `<h3>Processing reimbursements (seven-day rule${j.deadlines && j.deadlines.reimburse_provisional ? ', provisional' : ', sandbox rule approved 18 Nov 2026'})</h3><table class=\"st-table\"><tr><th>Order</th><th>Status</th><th>Amount</th><th>Paid (Irish date)</th><th>Due</th><th>Alerts and attempts</th></tr>${j.reimbursements.map(x => `<tr${x.overdue || x.failing ? ' class=\"st-warn\"' : ''}><td>${esc(x.reference)}<br><small>day ${x.day}</small></td><td>${esc(x.status_label)}${x.overdue ? '<br><strong>OVERDUE</strong>' : ''}</td><td>${esc(x.amount_label)}</td><td>${esc(x.payment_confirmed)}</td><td>${esc(x.due_label)}</td><td><small>${[x.alerts.day5 ? 'Day-5 alert sent' : '', x.alerts.deadline || x.alerts.extended_deadline ? 'Deadline alert sent' : '', x.delay_notice_at ? 'Delay notice sent to the artist (test sink)' : '', x.attempts ? `${x.attempts} failed attempt(s); last: ${x.last_error || ''}. Due date unchanged.` : '', ...x.flags].filter(Boolean).map(esc).join('<br>')}</small>${x.action ? `<br><button data-a=\"processing\" data-id=\"${esc(x.order_id)}\">Reconcile processing fee</button>` : ''}</td></tr>`).join('')}</table>` : ''}\n        <details><summary>How to pay a shortfall (bank details process)</summary><ol>${j.bank_details_process.map(x => `<li>${esc(x)}</li>`).join('')}</ol></details>`;\n      if (j.holds.length) h += `<h2>Legal holds</h2><ul>${j.holds.map(x => `<li data-hold=\"${esc(x.id)}\">${esc(x.reference)} · ${esc(x.basis)} · review by ${esc(x.review_by)}${x.review_overdue ? ' <strong>(review overdue)</strong>' : ''} — ${esc(x.reason)}\n        ${step('renew', 'Renew…', `${field(`hr-rv-${esc(x.id)}`, 'New review date (within 12 months)', `<input id=\"hr-rv-${esc(x.id)}\" name=\"review_by\" type=\"date\" min=\"${plusDaysIE(1)}\" max=\"${plusDaysIE(365)}\" required>`)}\n          ${field(`hr-why-${esc(x.id)}`, 'Why is the hold still needed? (10 characters or more)', `<textarea id=\"hr-why-${esc(x.id)}\" name=\"note\" rows=\"2\" maxlength=\"1000\" required></textarea>`)}`, 'Renew hold')}\n        ${step('release', 'Release…', `${field(`hl-why-${esc(x.id)}`, 'Why can it be released? (10 characters or more)', `<textarea id=\"hl-why-${esc(x.id)}\" name=\"note\" rows=\"2\" maxlength=\"1000\" required></textarea>`)}\n          ${tick('Release this hold. The order’s records then follow the normal retention rules.')}`, 'Release hold')}</li>`).join('')}</ul>`;\n      if (j.unprocessed_events.length) h += `<h2>Provider events waiting</h2><ul>${j.unprocessed_events.map(e => `<li>${esc(e.type)} · ${esc(e.status)} · ${esc(e.detail || '')}</li>`).join('')}</ul>`;\n    } else {\n      const m = j.membership;\n      if (!m.opted_in) h += j.addendum ? `<h2>Join the payment pilot (optional)</h2><p>Read the <a href=\"/payment-terms/${esc(j.addendum.doc_id)}.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">${esc(j.addendum.title)}</a>.</p>\n        <form data-f=\"optin\"><label><input type=\"checkbox\" name=\"accept\" required> ${esc(j.addendum.statement)}</label><button>Join the pilot</button></form>` : '<p>The payment addendum has not been issued yet.</p>';\n      else {\n        h += `<p class=\"st-muted\">${esc(j.direct_payment_note)}</p>`;\n        if (j.seller_profile && !j.checkout_available) h += `<p class=\"st-warn\">${esc(j.trader_question.unavailable)}</p>`;\n        const sp = j.seller_profile || {};\n        h += `<details ${j.seller_problems.length ? 'open' : ''}><summary>Seller information for managed checkout${j.seller_problems.length ? ' — needed before any managed-checkout quote' : ''}</summary><p>${esc(j.trader_question.direct)}</p><form data-f=\"seller\">\n          ${[['legal_name', 'Legal name'], ['trading_name', 'Trading name (optional)'], ['address', 'Address where you are established'], ['returns_address', 'Returns and complaints address, if different (optional)'], ['email', 'Email for buyers'], ['phone', 'Telephone for buyers'], ['vat_number', 'VAT number, if registered (optional)']]\n            .map(([k, t]) => `<label>${t} <input name=\"${k}\" value=\"${esc(sp[k] || '')}\"></label>`).join('')}\n          <fieldset><legend>${esc(j.trader_question.question)}</legend><p class=\"st-muted\"><em>${esc(j.trader_question.review_note)}</em></p><p class=\"st-muted\">${esc(j.trader_question.intro)}</p><p class=\"st-muted\">${esc(j.trader_question.explain)}</p>\n          ${j.trader_choices.map(c => `<label><input type=\"radio\" name=\"trader_status\" value=\"${esc(c.value)}\" required ${sp.trader_status === c.value ? 'checked' : ''}> <strong>${esc(c.label)}</strong><br><small>${esc(c.meaning)}</small></label>`).join('')}</fieldset>\n          <label><input type=\"checkbox\" name=\"confirm\" required> ${esc(j.seller_declaration)}</label><button>Save seller information</button></form></details>`;\n        if (j.pending_refunds.length) h += `<h2>A refund is waiting for your Stripe balance</h2>${j.pending_refunds.map(r => `<p class=\"st-warn\">${esc(r.reference)}: ${eur(r.amount_cents)}, waiting ${r.days_pending} days. Stripe cancels it on ${esc(r.stripe_fails_it_by)} if still unfunded.</p>`).join('')}<ol>${j.pending_refunds[0].what_to_do.map(x => `<li>${esc(x)}</li>`).join('')}</ol>`;\n        h += m.processing_consent ? `<p>You have agreed that Stripe’s processing fees may be deducted on commission-free pilot orders (${esc(m.processing_consent_at)}). <button data-a2=\"withdraw-processing\">Withdraw this consent</button></p>`\n          : `<details><summary>Commission-free sales through the pilot (optional, separate consent)</summary><form data-f=\"processing\"><label><input type=\"checkbox\" name=\"accept\" required> ${esc(j.processing_statement)}</label><button>Give this consent</button></form></details>`;\n        h += `<p>You joined the pilot on ${esc(m.opted_in_at)} (${esc(m.addendum)}). Stripe: ${m.account ? (m.ready ? (j.switches && j.switches.live ? 'ready to take payments' : 'ready to take test payments') : 'onboarding incomplete' + (m.account.requirements_due.length ? ' — Stripe still needs: ' + esc(m.account.requirements_due.join(', ')) : '')) : 'not connected yet'}.</p>\n          <p><button data-a2=\"onboard\">${m.account ? 'Continue Stripe onboarding' : 'Connect a Stripe account'}</button> ${m.account ? '<button data-a2=\"refresh\">Refresh status</button>' : ''}</p>`\n          + step('leave', 'Leave the payment pilot…', `<p class=\"st-muted\">Unpaid quotes are cancelled; paid orders continue to completion. Your seller information is removed (each issued quote keeps its own copy). You keep selling directly, as now, and can join again later.</p>\n            ${tick('Leave the payment pilot.')}`, 'Leave the pilot');\n      }\n    }\n    // multi-artist basket (separate, optional): artist controls and founder readiness\n    let bj = null;\n    try { bj = founder ? await api('GET', base + '/baskets/artists') : (j.membership && j.membership.opted_in ? await api('GET', base + '/basket') : null); } catch { bj = null; }\n    if (bj && bj.installed) h += founder ? basketFounder(bj) : basketArtist(bj, j);\n    h += `<h2>Orders</h2>${j.orders.length ? j.orders.map(orderCard).join('') : '<p class=\"st-muted\">None yet.</p>'}`;\n    app.innerHTML = h;\n    J_BASKET = bj;\n    wire(j);\n  }\n\n  function wire(j) {\n    const on = (sel, ev, fn) => app.querySelectorAll(sel).forEach(el => el.addEventListener(ev, act(fn)));\n    const idOf = el => el.closest('[data-id]').dataset.id;\n    on('form[data-f=\"create\"]', 'submit', async e => { const f = new FormData(e.target); await api('POST', base + '/orders', Object.fromEntries(f)); say('Draft created'); load(); });\n    on('form[data-f=\"edit\"]', 'submit', async e => { const f = new FormData(e.target);\n      await api('PUT', `${base}/orders/${idOf(e.target)}`, { artwork_cents: Number(f.get('artwork_cents')), delivery_cents: Number(f.get('delivery_cents')), delivery: JSON.parse(f.get('delivery')), exclusion: f.get('exclusion') || null });\n      say('Saved as a new quote version'); load(); });\n    on('form[data-f=\"pause\"]', 'submit', async e => { const f = new FormData(e.target); await api('POST', base + '/pause', { paused: true, return_on: f.get('return_on'), note: f.get('note') }); say('New quotes and payments paused'); load(); });\n    on('button[data-pause]', 'click', async () => { await api('POST', base + '/pause', { paused: false }); say('New quotes and payments resumed'); load(); });\n    on('button[data-alert-read]', 'click', async e => { await api('POST', `${base}/alerts/${e.target.dataset.alertRead}`, { read: e.target.dataset.v === '1' }); load(); });\n    on('button[data-alert-save]', 'click', async e => { const id = e.target.dataset.alertSave;\n      await api('POST', `${base}/alerts/${id}`, { next_action: app.querySelector(`[data-next=\"${id}\"]`).value, follow_up_on: app.querySelector(`[data-fu=\"${id}\"]`).value }); say('Next action saved'); load(); });\n    on('button[data-a]', 'click', async e => {\n      const id = idOf(e.target), a = e.target.dataset.a;\n      await api('POST', `${base}/orders/${id}/${a}`, {});\n      say('Done'); load(); });\n    on('form[data-f=\"issue\"]', 'submit', async e => { const f = new FormData(e.target), id = idOf(e.target);\n      const days = Number(f.get('days')), linked = f.get('linked');\n      if (!Number.isInteger(days) || days < 1 || days > 7) throw new Error('Enter how many days the quote is valid: a whole number from 1 to 7');\n      if (!linked) throw new Error('Answer the linked-purchases question');\n      const r = await api('POST', `${base}/orders/${id}/issue`, { days, linked_check_confirmed: linked === 'not_linked' });\n      ISSUED = { id, link: r.buyer_link, version: r.order && r.order.quote_version };\n      say('Buyer quote issued'); await load();\n      const box = app.querySelector('[data-issued] [data-link]'); if (box) { box.focus(); box.select(); } });\n    on('form[data-f=\"refund\"]', 'submit', async e => { const f = new FormData(e.target), id = idOf(e.target);\n      const artwork_cents = toCents(f.get('artwork'), 'artwork amount'), delivery_cents = toCents(f.get('delivery'), 'delivery amount'), reason = String(f.get('reason') || '').trim();\n      if (artwork_cents + delivery_cents === 0) throw new Error('Enter an artwork or delivery amount to refund');\n      if (reason.length < 3) throw new Error('Give a reason for the refund');\n      if (f.get('confirm') !== 'on') throw new Error('Tick the box to confirm the refund');\n      await api('POST', `${base}/orders/${id}/refund`, { artwork_cents, delivery_cents, reason }); say('Refund sent to Stripe'); load(); });\n    app.querySelectorAll('form[data-f=\"refund\"]').forEach(fm => { const sum = fm.querySelector('[data-sum]'), upd = () => {\n      try { const t = toCents(fm.artwork.value, 'artwork amount') + toCents(fm.delivery.value, 'delivery amount'); sum.textContent = t ? `The buyer will be refunded ${eur(t)}.` : ''; } catch { sum.textContent = ''; } };\n      fm.addEventListener('input', upd); upd(); });\n    app.querySelectorAll('[data-copy]').forEach(b => b.addEventListener('click', async () => { const box = b.closest('[data-issued]'), inp = box.querySelector('[data-link]'), note = box.querySelector('[data-copied]');\n      inp.focus(); inp.select();\n      try { await navigator.clipboard.writeText(inp.value); note.textContent = 'Copied.'; } catch { note.textContent = 'Selected: press Ctrl+C (or ⌘C) to copy.'; } }));\n    on('form[data-f=\"approve\"]', 'submit', async e => { const f = new FormData(e.target), id = idOf(e.target);\n      const confirm = Object.fromEntries(['available', 'location', 'condition', 'framing', 'dimensions', 'packing_and_handover', 'returns', 'seller_information'].map(k => [k, f.get(k) === 'on']));\n      await api('POST', `${base}/orders/${id}/approve`, { quote_version: j.orders.find(o => o.id === id).quote_version, confirm, note: f.get('note') }); say('Approved'); load(); });\n    on('form[data-f=\"fulfil\"]', 'submit', async e => { const f = new FormData(e.target); await api('POST', `${base}/orders/${idOf(e.target)}/fulfilment`, Object.fromEntries(f)); say('Recorded'); load(); });\n    on('form[data-f=\"seller\"]', 'submit', async e => { const f = new FormData(e.target); await api('PUT', base + '/seller-profile', { ...Object.fromEntries(f), confirm: f.get('confirm') === 'on' }); say('Seller information saved'); load(); });\n    on('form[data-f=\"optin\"]', 'submit', async () => { await api('POST', base + '/opt-in', { accept: true, doc_id: j.addendum.doc_id, html_sha256: j.addendum.html_sha256 }); say('You joined the pilot'); load(); });\n    on('form[data-f=\"basket-optin\"]', 'submit', async () => { const b = J_BASKET; await api('POST', base + '/basket/opt-in', { accept: true, doc_id: b.addendum.doc_id, html_sha256: b.addendum.html_sha256 }); say('You are taking part in the basket'); load(); });\n    on('form[data-f=\"basket-disclosure\"]', 'submit', async () => { const b = J_BASKET; await api('POST', base + '/basket/seller-disclosure', { accept: true, statement: b.disclosure_statement, subject_sha256: b.seller_info.subject_sha256 }); say('Confirmed'); load(); });\n    on('form[data-f=\"basket-processing\"]', 'submit', async () => { const b = J_BASKET; await api('POST', base + '/basket/processing-consent', { accept: true, statement: b.processing_statement }); say('Consent recorded'); load(); });\n    on('form[data-f=\"offer\"]', 'submit', async e => { const f = new FormData(e.target), id = e.target.querySelector('[data-id]').dataset.id, F = J_BASKET.delivery_fields, d = {};\n      need(f.get('confirm') === 'on', 'Tick the box to confirm the delivery offer');\n      for (const [k, t] of Object.entries(F)) { if (k === 'destination') continue; const raw = String(f.get(k) ?? '').trim(), ty = typeof t === 'string' ? t.replace('?', '') : t;\n        if (!raw) { d[k] = null; continue; }\n        d[k] = CENTS.includes(k) ? toCents(raw, label(k)) : ty === 'n' ? Number(raw.replace(',', '.')) : ty === 'b' ? raw === 'true' : raw; }\n      await api('PUT', `${base}/basket/offers/${encodeURIComponent(id)}`, { confirm: true, delivery_cents: toCents(f.get('charge'), 'delivery charge'), delivery: d }); say('Delivery offer saved'); load(); });\n    on('button[data-withdraw-offer]', 'click', async e => { await api('DELETE', `${base}/basket/offers/${encodeURIComponent(e.target.dataset.withdrawOffer)}`); say('Delivery offer withdrawn'); load(); });\n    on('form[data-f=\"basket-leave\"]', 'submit', async (e) => { need(new FormData(e.target).get('confirm') === 'on', 'Tick the box to confirm'); await api('POST', base + '/basket/leave', {}); say('Online purchase stopped'); load(); });\n    on('form[data-f=\"processing\"]', 'submit', async () => { await api('POST', base + '/processing-consent', { accept: true, statement: j.processing_statement }); say('Consent recorded'); load(); });\n    const F = (kind, fn) => on(`form[data-f=\"${kind}\"]`, 'submit', async e => fn(e, new FormData(e.target), e.target));\n    const noteOf = (f, min, what) => { const t = String(f.get('note') || '').trim(); need(t.length >= min, what); return t; };\n    F('hold', async (e, f) => { const basis = f.get('basis'), reason = String(f.get('reason') || '').trim(), review_by = f.get('review_by');\n      need(basis, 'Choose the basis for the hold'); need(reason.length >= 10, 'Give the specific reason for the hold (10–1,000 characters)'); need(isDate(review_by), 'Give a review date within the next 12 months');\n      await api('POST', `${base}/orders/${idOf(e.target)}/hold`, { basis, reason, review_by }); say('Legal hold placed'); load(); });\n    F('repaid', async (e, f) => { const artwork_cents = toCents(f.get('artwork'), 'artwork amount'), delivery_cents = toCents(f.get('delivery'), 'delivery amount'), evidence = String(f.get('evidence') || '').trim();\n      need(artwork_cents + delivery_cents > 0, 'Enter the artwork or delivery amount repaid'); need(evidence.length >= 10, 'Describe the evidence (bank transfer reference, date, and the buyer’s confirmation)');\n      need(f.get('confirm') === 'on', 'Tick the box to confirm the repayment');\n      await api('POST', `${base}/orders/${idOf(e.target)}/repaid`, { artwork_cents, delivery_cents, evidence }); say('Repayment recorded'); load(); });\n    F('shortfallpaid', async (e, f) => { const amount_cents = toCents(f.get('amount'), 'amount paid'), executed_on = f.get('executed_on'), reference = String(f.get('reference') || '').trim();\n      need(amount_cents > 0, 'Enter the amount the bank shows as executed'); need(isDate(executed_on), 'Give the date the bank shows the transfer as executed');\n      need(executed_on <= todayIE(), 'The execution date cannot be in the future: record the payment once the bank shows it executed');\n      need(reference.length >= 6, 'Give the bank’s transfer reference (6–200 characters)'); need(f.get('confirm') === 'on', 'Tick the box to confirm the bank shows the transfer as executed');\n      await api('POST', `${base}/orders/${idOf(e.target)}/shortfallpaid`, { amount_cents, executed_on, reference }); say('Shortfall payment recorded'); load(); });\n    F('shortfallreturned', async (e, f) => { const returned_on = f.get('returned_on'), reason = String(f.get('reason') || '').trim();\n      need(isDate(returned_on), 'Give the date the bank shows the transfer as returned'); need(reason.length >= 5, 'Give the reason the bank gave (5–300 characters, no bank details)');\n      need(f.get('confirm') === 'on', 'Tick the box to confirm the bank shows the transfer as returned');\n      await api('POST', `${base}/orders/${idOf(e.target)}/shortfallreturned`, { payment_id: f.get('payment_id'), returned_on, reason }); say('Returned transfer recorded'); load(); });\n    F('returncommission', async (e, f) => { const reason = String(f.get('reason') || '').trim();\n      need(reason.length >= 3, 'Give a reason'); need(f.get('confirm') === 'on', 'Tick the box to confirm the commission return');\n      await api('POST', `${base}/orders/${idOf(e.target)}/refund`, { commission_only: true, reason }); say('Commission returned'); load(); });\n    F('cancel', async (e, f) => { need(f.get('confirm') === 'on', 'Tick the box to confirm the cancellation');\n      await api('POST', `${base}/orders/${idOf(e.target)}/cancel`, { reason: String(f.get('reason') || '').trim() }); say('Order cancelled'); load(); });\n    F('decline', async (e, f) => { const id = idOf(e.target);\n      await api('POST', `${base}/orders/${id}/approve`, { decision: 'decline', quote_version: j.orders.find(o => o.id === id).quote_version, note: String(f.get('note') || '').trim() }); say('Sent back to PlotArt for changes'); load(); });\n    F('renew', async (e, f) => { const id = e.target.closest('[data-hold]').dataset.hold, review_by = f.get('review_by');\n      need(isDate(review_by), 'Give a new review date within the next 12 months'); const note = noteOf(f, 10, 'Record why the hold is still needed (10 characters or more)');\n      await api('POST', `${base}/holds/${id}`, { decision: 'renew', review_by, note }); say('Hold renewed'); load(); });\n    F('release', async (e, f) => { const id = e.target.closest('[data-hold]').dataset.hold, note = noteOf(f, 10, 'Record why the hold can be released (10 characters or more)');\n      need(f.get('confirm') === 'on', 'Tick the box to confirm the release');\n      await api('POST', `${base}/holds/${id}`, { decision: 'release', note }); say('Hold released'); load(); });\n    F('leave', async (e, f) => { need(f.get('confirm') === 'on', 'Tick the box to confirm you are leaving the pilot');\n      await api('POST', `${base}/leave`, {}); say('You left the payment pilot'); load(); });\n    app.querySelectorAll('a[data-open]').forEach(a => a.addEventListener('click', () => {\n      const d = app.querySelector(`#order-${CSS.escape(a.getAttribute('href').slice(7))} details[data-step=\"${a.dataset.open}\"]`); if (d) { d.open = true; setTimeout(() => d.querySelector('input, textarea, select')?.focus(), 0); } }));\n    on('button[data-a2]', 'click', async e => { const a = e.target.dataset.a2;\n      if (a === 'withdraw-basket-processing') { await api('POST', base + '/basket/processing-consent/withdraw', {}); say('Consent withdrawn'); load(); return; }\n      if (a === 'withdraw-disclosure') { await api('POST', base + '/basket/seller-disclosure/withdraw', {}); say('Withdrawn'); load(); return; }\n      if (a === 'withdraw-processing') { await api('POST', base + '/processing-consent/withdraw', {}); load(); return; }\n      if (a === 'onboard') { const r = await api('POST', base + '/onboarding', {}); location.href = r.url; return; }\n      if (a === 'refresh') { await api('POST', `${base}/account/refresh`, {}); load(); } });\n    on('button[data-refresh]', 'click', async e => { await api('POST', `${base}/accounts/${e.target.dataset.refresh}/refresh`, {}); load(); });\n  }\n  load().catch(e => { app.innerHTML = `<p>${esc(e.message)}</p>`; });\n})();\n";
